/* Kamome House, Season 1: one optional episode per Japanese Foundations unit (story bible Draft 4, with the owner's later arrival dates:
   Mariya last April; Cheska and Toby last October; Rodrigo, Kaito, Yến and Aoi new this April).
   Parts: narr (Mugi's English narration) · line (who, ja, en, gl = gloss for words above level) · note (Mugi's one inline note)
   · plates (tap-to-read cards) · ex (an ordinary exercise, any engine type) · lang (language in context) · reflect.
   draft:true episodes show only with #story-<unit>?draft (for the owner's review). */
window.ICA_STORY = {
  cast: {  // art: has a six-mood sheet in shared/cast/<id>/<mood>.webp (hello, think, oops, yay, tip, sleepy); acc: accent colour
    cheska:{name:"Cheska", ja:"チェスカ", art:true, acc:"#7a8450"}, yen:{name:"Yến", ja:"イエン", art:true, acc:"#2f8a8a"},
    rodrigo:{name:"Rodrigo", ja:"ロドリゴ", art:true, acc:"#b8573a"}, toby:{name:"Toby", ja:"トビー", art:true, acc:"#5b9bd5"},
    aoi:{name:"Aoi", ja:"あおい", art:true, acc:"#7d3c5c"}, mariya:{name:"Mariya", ja:"まりや", art:true, acc:"#e8735f"}, kaito:{name:"Kaito", ja:"かいと", art:true, acc:"#3f4a8a"},
    fumiko:{name:"Mrs Satō", ja:"さとうさん", art:true, acc:"#9b86c2"}, shoichi:{name:"Mr Satō", ja:"さとうさん", art:true, acc:"#c9a03c"},
    chiyo:{name:"Chiyo", ja:"ちよさん", acc:"#8c7a5b"}, siti:{name:"Siti", ja:"シティ", acc:"#5f8f86"},  // supporting cast with several lines (no art)
    matsumoto:{name:"Mr Matsumoto", ja:"まつもとさん", acc:"#6f7f8f"}, hiroyuki:{name:"Hiroyuki", ja:"ひろゆき", acc:"#7a6a58"}, megumi:{name:"Megumi", ja:"めぐみ", acc:"#a0707e"},
    sota:{name:"Sōta", ja:"そうた", acc:"#7d9a5f"}, kuze:{name:"Kaito's father", ja:"かいとの父", acc:"#5c6478"}
  },
  episodes: [
  {unit:"e3u1", n:1, title:"Names on the mailboxes", month:"April", level:"Kana only", parts:[
    {t:"narr", text:"Ngô Hải Yến gets off the bus with two suitcases and a printed map she turns out not to need. It is April in Shioura, a harbour town on the Sea of Japan coast, and the house is exactly where the map says: old, wooden, two storeys, with the sea somewhere behind it making itself heard."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Before she finds a doorbell, she finds the mailboxes. Eight of them hang by the gate, family names only, the way mailboxes in Japan usually are. Some labels are crisp. Some have been through a winter. One, in a stranger's careful handwriting, is already hers."},
    {t:"mailboxes", title:"The mailboxes", hint:"Read each name, then tap the mailbox to check.", items:[
      {room:"101", ja:"ベルガラ", ro:"Vergara", old:true, who:"Cheska Vergara, from the Philippines. She moved in last October, and her label has had a winter of sea air to prove it. Japanese has no *v*, so katakana borrows the ば row: ベ for *ve*."},
      {room:"102", ja:"モンドラゴン", ro:"Mondragón", who:"Rodrigo Mondragón, from Mexico. New this April; the ink still looks wet. Six beats, two of them ン: モ・ン・ド・ラ・ゴ・ン."},
      {room:"103", ja:"せと", ro:"Seto", old:true, who:"Mariya Seto, from an island an hour away by ferry. She has been here a year, which at twenty makes her the house veteran. Two short beats: せ・と."},
      {room:"201", ja:"ウィットロック", ro:"Whitlock", old:true, who:"Toby Whitlock, from Australia. He moved in last October, the same week as Cheska, and his name only just fits on the label. ウィ is how katakana writes *wi*, and each small ッ is a one-beat pause: ウィ・ッ・ト・ロ・ッ・ク."},
      {room:"202", ja:"とがわ", ro:"Togawa", who:"Aoi Togawa, a master's student from Saitama. New this April. Three beats: と・が・わ. The two small strokes on が turn *ka* into *ga*."},
      {room:"203", ja:"くぜ", ro:"Kuze", who:"Kaito Kuze, a first-year student from a mountain town. New this April. He wrote the label himself, very small, as if hoping the post might not notice him. Two beats: く・ぜ."},
      {room:"204", ja:"ゴー", ro:"Ngô", who:"Ngô Hải Yến, from Vietnam. New today. Katakana can't spell the *ng* at the start, so Ngô becomes ゴー, and the ー stretches the vowel to two beats. She looks at it for a while. It is the shortest she has ever been."},
      {room:"205", ja:"", ro:"(empty)", who:"Room 205. No name on the label, and a slot that still gets its share of pizza flyers."}],
      cottage:{ja:"さとう", ro:"Satō", who:"Mr and Mrs Satō, who own the house and live in the cottage across the garden. Three beats, not two: さ・と・う. The う stretches the *o*."}},
    {t:"narr", text:"Above the gate there is a wooden sign: かもめそう. *Kamome* is a seagull, and *-sō* is how a lot of small apartment houses end their names. An actual seagull is sitting on the sign, which seems like overdoing it."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Someone is coming down the path at speed. This is Mariya, from Room 103, who has lived here a year and has spent most of it waiting for somebody new to explain the rubbish to. She begins before Yến has let go of the suitcases."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Yến learned her Japanese in four years of meetings with clients. Mariya's is the fast, friendly kind nobody uses in meetings. Yến catches about half of the words and all of the pointing."},
    {t:"gomi", title:"The rubbish station", hint:"Tap a bag to see what goes in it. Every town has its own rules (some have more than twenty types); these are Shioura's main ones.", items:[
      {icon:"bag", ja:"もえるごみ", ro:"moeru gomi", en:"burnable rubbish", when:"Mon and Thu", note:"Food waste (なまごみ: drain it and wrap it in newspaper first), paper tissues and anything else that burns, in the city's own see-through bags."},
      {icon:"cup", ja:"もえないごみ", ro:"moenai gomi", en:"non-burnable rubbish", when:"2nd and 4th Wed", note:"Broken crockery, small metal things, light bulbs. Wrap anything sharp and write きけん (danger) on the bag."},
      {icon:"pla", ja:"プラ", ro:"pura", en:"plastic packaging", when:"Tue", note:"Anything with the プラ mark: wrappers, trays, bags, bottle caps. Rinse it first."},
      {icon:"pet", ja:"ペットボトル", ro:"petto botoru", en:"plastic (PET) drink bottles", when:"1st and 3rd Wed", note:"Bottles with the PET mark. Caps and labels off (they go in プラ), rinsed and squashed."},
      {icon:"can", ja:"びん・かん", ro:"bin, kan", en:"glass bottles and cans", when:"1st and 3rd Wed", note:"Glass bottles and drink or food cans, rinsed. Spray cans must be completely empty."},
      {icon:"box", ja:"ダンボール・しんぶん", ro:"danbōru, shinbun", en:"cardboard and newspaper", when:"Fri", note:"Flattened cardboard boxes, newspapers and magazines, tied with string. Paper is a resource, so it isn't burnable rubbish here."},
      {icon:"chair", ja:"そだいごみ", ro:"sodai gomi", en:"oversized items", when:"By booking", note:"Furniture, bikes, big appliances. Book a pickup with the city and buy a fee sticker at a convenience store. Air conditioners, TVs, fridges and washing machines follow a separate recycling law."}],
      calendar:[["月","げつ","もえるごみ"],["火","か","プラ"],["水","すい","びん・かん・ペットボトル (1st and 3rd), もえないごみ (2nd and 4th)"],["木","もく","もえるごみ"],["金","きん","ダンボール・しんぶん"]],
      calnote:"Days of the week are written with kanji; the small kana above each one show how to read it. Rubbish goes out by 8 in the morning on its day, never the night before. Food waste goes out twice a week, with the burnables."},
    {t:"note", text:"Everyone expects the first thing they'll read in Japan to be a menu. It's a mailbox. Then a rubbish calendar. The menu has pictures; it can wait."},
    {t:"narr", text:"An old man crosses the garden from the cottage with an umbrella under his arm. This is Mr Satō. He studies the sky, which is the same grey as the sea, and delivers his verdict in one word: あめ."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Yến knows あめ. She glances round for the sweets, and only then hears the tune again in her head: high, then down. That's rain. Candy would have stayed up. Same two kana, different melody. He hooks the umbrella over her suitcase handle and goes back the way he came."},
    {t:"narr", text:"A black-and-white cat has watched all of this from the wall. Yến says ミウ, quietly, which is what you call a cat where she comes from. The cat looks at her. Mariya sings out ムゥ, and the cat looks at Mariya. There seems to be room in the cat for both."},
    {t:"cat", pose:"curious", alt:"The black-and-white cat, looking up from the wall"},
    {t:"narr", text:"Then it rains, as promised."},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u1-x1", type:"mcq", q:"Which mailbox belongs to Toby Whitlock?", options:[
      {t:"ウィットロック", ok:true, why:"Right: ウィ (*wi*), ッ (a pause), ト, ロ, ッ, ク."},
      {t:"ウイトロク", why:"Close, but this has no pauses. Whitlock has two: a small ッ before ト and another before ク."},
      {t:"モンドラゴン", why:"That's Rodrigo Mondragón, in Room 102."},
      {t:"ゴー", why:"That's Yến's family name, Ngô."}]}},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u1-x2", type:"mcq", q:"The plate on the cottage says さとう. How many beats (morae) does it have?", options:[
      {t:"Three", ok:true, why:"さ・と・う: the long *o* takes a beat of its own."},
      {t:"Two", why:"Two beats would be さと, like せと (Seto) on Mariya's mailbox. In さとう the う stretches the vowel and counts as a beat."},
      {t:"Four", why:"There are only three kana here, and each is one beat."}]}},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u1-x4", type:"mcq", q:"Yến's first piece of rubbish at Kamome House is the empty plastic tray from her lunch on the train. It has the プラ mark on it. Which bag does it go in?", options:[
      {t:"プラ", ok:true, why:"Right: the プラ mark means plastic packaging, which has its own collection day (火, *ka*, Tuesday, on this calendar). Mariya would want it rinsed first."},
      {t:"もえるごみ", why:"Not in Shioura: plastic packaging with the プラ mark is collected separately. Some cities do burn it, which is why you always check the local rules."},
      {t:"ペットボトル", why:"That bag is only for PET drink bottles. A tray isn't a bottle."},
      {t:"びん・かん", why:"That's for glass bottles and cans."}]}},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u1-x3", type:"type", q:"The sign above the gate says *Kamome-sō*. Type it in hiragana.", book:"Write *Kamome-sō* in hiragana.", answer:"かもめそう",
      hint:"The long *o* is written with う in hiragana.",
      wrongs:[{v:"かもめそ", why:"The *o* in *sō* is long, so it needs a second kana: そう."},{v:"かもめそお", why:"A long *o* is usually written with う, not お: そう."}],
      why:"かもめそう: か・も・め・そ・う, five beats. Hiragana writes the long *o* with う."}},
    {t:"lang", items:["Long vowels: さとう (*Satō*, three beats) and せと (*Seto*, two beats) look alike at a glance, but the extra beat makes a different name.", "Small ッ: the pause in ウィットロック counts as a beat, just like the one in きって.", "Pitch: あめ (rain) starts high and drops; あめ (candy) starts low and stays up. The kana are identical, so only your ear can tell them apart."]},
    {t:"reflect", q:"Which nameplate took you longest to read, and what made it hard?"}
  ]},
  {unit:"e3u2", n:2, title:"はじめまして", month:"April", level:"N5", parts:[
    {t:"narr", text:"The first Sunday in April. On Sundays the Satōs cross the garden and eat with the house, and Mrs Satō does the cooking, because she has seen what students cook."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Cheska has lived here since October and is on table duty, which is as close to the cooking as she plans to get. Her assistant is the new man from Room 102. He arrived late last night and has been waiting all day for somebody to introduce himself to."},
    {t:"line", mood:"yay", who:"rodrigo", ja:"はじめまして！ロドリゴです！メキシコから[来]{き}ました！", en:"Nice to meet you! I'm Rodrigo! I'm from Mexico!"},
    {t:"narr", text:"Rodrigo learned his Japanese from anime. Every word of it is correct, and it comes out the way a hero introduces himself to a rival on a rooftop."},
    {t:"line", who:"cheska", ja:"はじめまして。チェスカです。フィリピンから[来]{き}ました。", en:"Nice to meet you. I'm Cheska. From the Philippines."},
    {t:"line", who:"rodrigo", ja:"よろしくお[願]{ねが}いします！", en:"Good to meet you!", gl:"よろしくお願いします: what you say after your name when you meet someone. Roughly \"please be good to me\"."},
    {t:"narr", text:"She hands him a jar of chopsticks. Nobody in this house has matching ones, so every pair has an owner, and Rodrigo is a man who likes to know whose things he is touching."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"rodrigo", ja:"これはだれのはしですか。", en:"Whose chopsticks are these?", gl:"はし: chopsticks."},
    {t:"line", who:"cheska", ja:"それはトビーさんのです。", en:"Those are Toby's."},
    {t:"line", who:"rodrigo", ja:"これは？", en:"And these?"},
    {t:"line", who:"cheska", ja:"まりやさんのです。", en:"Mariya's."},
    {t:"narr", text:"At the bottom of the stack of plates he finds a small chipped saucer with a fish painted on it."},
    {t:"line", who:"rodrigo", ja:"これは？", en:"And this?"},
    {t:"line", who:"cheska", ja:"それはミンミンのです。", en:"That's Mingming's."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"rodrigo", ja:"ミンミンさんはだれですか。[学生]{がくせい}ですか。", en:"Who's Mingming? A student?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"cheska", ja:"いいえ、[学生]{がくせい}じゃありません。ねこです。", en:"No, not a student. A cat."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Mrs Satō comes through with a dish in each hand and stops for exactly as long as this takes."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"fumiko", ja:"ミンミンじゃありません。ねこさんです。", en:"She isn't Mingming. She's Neko-san.", gl:"ねこさん: \"Ms Cat\", which is Mrs Satō's name for her."},
    {t:"note", text:"The cat belongs to nobody, turns up every evening, and is called something different by everyone who feeds her. Mrs Satō keeps a tally of the names on the noticeboard. She keeps it in pencil."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Then the food starts to arrive, faster than anyone can identify it. Rodrigo begins with the bowl under his nose: a heap of tiny purple creatures, whole, each looking back at him."},
    {t:"line", who:"rodrigo", ja:"これは[何]{なん}ですか。", en:"What's this?"},
    {t:"line", who:"cheska", ja:"それはいかです。", en:"That's squid.", gl:"いか: squid. These are firefly squid, a spring thing on this coast, about the length of a thumb."},
    {t:"line", who:"rodrigo", ja:"あれは？", en:"And that, over there?"},
    {t:"line", who:"cheska", ja:"あれはとり[肉]{にく}です。", en:"That's chicken.", gl:"とり肉: chicken (とり, bird + 肉, meat)."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"fumiko", ja:"とり[肉]{にく}じゃありません。たこですよ。", en:"It isn't chicken. It's octopus, you know.", gl:"たこ: octopus (here, deep-fried). よ at the end means \"I'm telling you something you don't know\"."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Cheska has had six months of Sundays and a great deal of that chicken. She takes the news without blinking. She is good in a crisis."},
    {t:"narr", text:"One dish is left. It is grey, speckled, cut into triangles, and it trembles slightly when Rodrigo leans on the table."},
    {t:"line", who:"rodrigo", ja:"じゃあ、これは？", en:"All right, and this?"},
    {t:"line", who:"cheska", ja:"それはこんにゃくです。", en:"That's konnyaku.", gl:"こんにゃく: a firm grey jelly made from the root of the konjac plant. It tastes mostly of whatever it was cooked in."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"rodrigo", ja:"こんにゃくは[何]{なん}ですか。[魚]{さかな}ですか。", en:"What's konnyaku? Is it fish?"},
    {t:"line", who:"cheska", ja:"[魚]{さかな}じゃありません。", en:"It isn't fish."},
    {t:"line", who:"rodrigo", ja:"[肉]{にく}ですか。", en:"Meat?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"cheska", ja:"[肉]{にく}じゃありません。こんにゃくは…こんにゃくです。", en:"It isn't meat. Konnyaku is... konnyaku."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Slippers on the steep stairs. The rest of the house comes down in ones and twos, and Rodrigo gets to his feet for every one of them. You can only say はじめまして to a person once, and he doesn't intend to waste any."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"yen", ja:"はじめまして。ゴー・ハイ・イエンと[申]{もう}します。どうぞよろしくお[願]{ねが}いいたします。", en:"How do you do. My name is Ngô Hải Yến. I look forward to working with you.", gl:"と申します and お願いいたします: the very formal, business-meeting versions of です and お願いします."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Yến spent four years in meetings with Japanese clients, and this is the only way she has ever been introduced. Behind her, Mariya from Room 103 has gone pink with the effort of not laughing."},
    {t:"line", who:"kaito", ja:"…くぜです。", en:"...Kuze."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Kaito is nineteen and says this to the tatami. Mr Satō comes in last, taps the barometer in the hall on his way past, and sits down looking satisfied with whatever it told him."},
    {t:"line", who:"fumiko", ja:"じゃあ、[食]{た}べましょう。", en:"Right. Let's eat."},
    {t:"line", who:"Everyone", ja:"いただきます。", en:"Itadakimasu.", gl:"いただきます: said before every meal. It thanks everyone and everything that went into the food."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Rodrigo says it half a beat late and twice as loud. Then, because he is not a man to leave a question open, he takes a triangle of konnyaku. Cheska watches him chew."},
    {t:"line", who:"cheska", ja:"おいしいですか。", en:"Is it good?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"rodrigo", ja:"……こんにゃくです。", en:"...It's konnyaku."},
    {t:"narr", text:"There is a small sound at the window. Something black and white is sitting on the sill, looking at a chipped saucer."},
    {t:"cat", pose:"smug", alt:"The cat on the windowsill, looking pleased with herself"},
    {t:"line", mood:"yay", who:"rodrigo", ja:"あ、ねこがいます！ミチ！", en:"Oh, there's a cat! Michi!", gl:"ミチ: *michi*, what you call a cat in Mexico. ねこがいます: \"there is a cat\" (います is for people and animals)."},
    {t:"narr", text:"The cat looks at him. Mrs Satō puts down her chopsticks and goes to find her pencil."},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u2-x1", type:"mcq", q:"Who is ミンミン?", options:[
      {t:"The cat", ok:true, why:"Right. Cheska says ねこです. ミンミン is Cheska's name for her; Mrs Satō insists on ねこさん, and by the end of dinner Rodrigo has added ミチ."},
      {t:"A student in the house", why:"That was Rodrigo's guess ([学生]{がくせい}ですか), and Cheska answered いいえ、[学生]{がくせい}じゃありません."},
      {t:"Mrs Satō", why:"Mrs Satō is the one who objects to the name: ミンミンじゃありません。ねこさんです."},
      {t:"The owner of the chopsticks", why:"The chopsticks were Toby's and Mariya's (トビーさんのです, まりやさんのです). ミンミン owns the saucer."}]}},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u2-x2", type:"mcq", q:"Cheska says あれはとり[肉]{にく}です. What is the dish really?", options:[
      {t:"たこ", ok:true, why:"Right. Mrs Satō corrects her: とり[肉]{にく}じゃありません。たこですよ. It isn't chicken; it's octopus."},
      {t:"とり[肉]{にく}", why:"That's what Cheska has believed for six months, but Mrs Satō says とり[肉]{にく}じゃありません: it is not chicken."},
      {t:"いか", why:"The squid was the first bowl, the one right in front of Rodrigo (これ). This dish is further away (あれ)."},
      {t:"こんにゃく", why:"Konnyaku is the grey, trembling one, and nobody mistakes it for chicken."}]}},
    {t:"lang", items:["これ・それ・あれ: Rodrigo asks about the bowl in front of him with これ, Cheska answers about the same bowl with それ (it is near him, not her), and the plate far from both of them is あれ.", "じゃありません: the everyday negative of です. [学生]{がくせい}じゃありません, とり[肉]{にく}じゃありません, [魚]{さかな}じゃありません. Three wrong guesses, three polite corrections.", "の without the noun: それはトビーさんのです (*that's Toby's*). Once everyone knows you mean the chopsticks, you can leave them out."]},
    {t:"reflect", q:"Rodrigo stands up and says はじめまして to every person who comes down the stairs. What do you do when you walk into a room full of people you don't know yet?"}
  ]},
  {unit:"e3u3", n:3, title:"The rules on the door", month:"April", level:"N5", parts:[
    {t:"narr", text:"Monday morning. Rodrigo arrived late on Saturday night, so he missed the tour Mrs Satō gives every new resident. Nobody is allowed to miss the tour. It starts at eight, at the bathroom door."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Kamome House has one bath and seven people. The answer is taped to the door: a timetable ruled in pencil by a retired primary-school teacher, seven names, twenty minutes each. Somebody in Room 202 has already underlined her own slot twice."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"fumiko", ja:"おふろは[一人]{ひとり}[二十分]{にじゅっぷん}です。ロドリゴさんは[午後]{ごご}[九時]{くじ}から[九時二十分]{くじにじゅっぷん}までです。", en:"The bath is twenty minutes each. Yours is from 9 to 9:20 in the evening, Rodrigo.", gl:"おふろ: the bath."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Last to arrive, last in the bath. Rodrigo doesn't mind; he respects a schedule. He does have questions."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"rodrigo", ja:"[朝]{あさ}、[入]{はい}ってもいいですか。", en:"May I have a bath in the morning?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"fumiko", ja:"[朝]{あさ}はシャワーだけです。", en:"Mornings are showers only.", gl:"だけ: only."},
    {t:"line", mood:"yay", who:"rodrigo", ja:"おふろで[歌]{うた}ってもいいですか。", en:"May I sing in the bath?", gl:"歌う (うたう): to sing."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"fumiko", ja:"…[小]{ちい}さい[声]{こえ}で[歌]{うた}ってください。", en:"...Please sing in a small voice.", gl:"声 (こえ): voice."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Nobody has ever asked Rodrigo for a small voice before. He reads the last line on the door, the one in red."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"rodrigo", ja:"「おふろでねてはいけません」。だれがねましたか。", en:"\"No sleeping in the bath.\" Who slept?", gl:"ねる: to sleep."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"fumiko", ja:"トビーさんです。", en:"Toby."},
    {t:"narr", text:"As if he had been called, Toby from Room 201 comes down the stairs: here since October, and the easiest person in the house to get along with. He comes down sideways, one hand on the wall."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"toby", ja:"おはようございます。あ、その[話]{はなし}ですか。[一回]{いっかい}だけですよ。", en:"Morning. Ah, that story. It was only the once."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"fumiko", ja:"[二回]{にかい}です。", en:"Twice."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"toby", ja:"…[二回]{にかい}です。", en:"...Twice."},
    {t:"narr", text:"The stairs have earned the sideways. They are stairs the way old Japanese houses build them, closer to a ladder than a staircase. Rodrigo looks up them with the joy of a man who has been shown a mountain."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"fumiko", ja:"このかいだんはあぶないですから、[走]{はし}らないでください。", en:"These stairs are dangerous, so please don't run.", gl:"かいだん: stairs. あぶない: dangerous."},
    {t:"line", mood:"yay", who:"rodrigo", ja:"わかった！[走]{はし}らない！やくそくだ！", en:"Got it! I won't run! That's a promise!", gl:"やくそく: a promise."},
    {t:"narr", text:"This is exactly how a hero accepts a mission. Mrs Satō taught seven-year-olds for thirty-five years."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"fumiko", ja:"「わかった」じゃありません。「わかりました」です。", en:"Not *wakatta*. *Wakarimashita*."},
    {t:"note", text:"わかった and わかりました mean the same thing. What changes is who you can say them to. The short plain forms are for friends, family and rivals on rooftops; a landlady gets ます. Mrs Satō will tell you this once, kindly. After that you are expected to know."},
    {t:"line", mood:"yay", who:"rodrigo", ja:"わかりました！", en:"Understood!"},
    {t:"narr", text:"The volume has not changed. She lets the volume go; volume isn't grammar. But she gives the stairs one more look before she moves on. Her husband is seventy-eight, and he climbs them whenever he thinks she isn't watching."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Next, the city office. Anyone who moves has fourteen days to tell the city where they live now, and Mrs Satō says she is going that way anyway. She is not. At the stop she tells him the bus is at 9:12. He already knows, and also knows that the 9:27 goes the long way round by the harbour. She looks at him with new interest."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Inside, nothing happens to you until you have a number."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"fumiko", ja:"ここをおしてください。", en:"Press here, please.", gl:"おす: to push, to press."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"rodrigo", ja:"[四十七番]{よんじゅうななばん}です。[今]{いま}、[何番]{なんばん}ですか。", en:"It's number 47. What number are they on now?", gl:"～番 (ばん): number ～, in a queue or a list."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"fumiko", ja:"[三十一番]{さんじゅういちばん}です。すわって、[待]{ま}ってください。", en:"Thirty-one. Please sit down and wait.", gl:"すわる: to sit."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Sixteen numbers to go. Rodrigo would rather wait standing, arms folded. He sits. She hands him the form: family name, given name, and an address he has had for two days."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"rodrigo", ja:"この[万年筆]{まんねんひつ}で[書]{か}いてもいいですか。", en:"May I write with this fountain pen?", gl:"万年筆 (まんねんひつ): a fountain pen."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"fumiko", ja:"…[黒]{くろ}いインクですか。", en:"...Is the ink black?", gl:"黒い (くろい): black. インク: ink."},
    {t:"line", mood:"yay", who:"rodrigo", ja:"[黒]{くろ}です！", en:"It's black!"},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"fumiko", ja:"じゃあ、[書]{か}いてもいいです。", en:"Then you may."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Rodrigo draws only with fountain pens, and owns eleven inks. He fills in the form slowly and beautifully. Then, with fourteen numbers still to go, he opens his notebook. Mrs Satō notices. Mrs Satō notices everything."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"fumiko", ja:"[何]{なに}をかいていますか。", en:"What are you drawing?", gl:"かく: here, to draw. It sounds the same as 書く, to write."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"rodrigo", ja:"…さとうさんをかいています。", en:"...I'm drawing you, Mrs Satō."},
    {t:"narr", text:"She holds out her hand for the notebook, as she must have for thirty-five years of notes passed in class. It is her, in about nine lines: the straight back, the handbag upright on her knees like a small, well-behaved dog. She looks at it for the length of two numbers."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"fumiko", ja:"…もう[一枚]{いちまい}かいてください。しゅじんに[見]{み}せたいです。", en:"...Please draw one more. I want to show my husband.", gl:"もう一枚: one more (sheet). しゅじん: my husband. 見せる: to show."},
    {t:"narr", text:"She does not correct anything. There is, apparently, nothing to correct."},
    {t:"narr", text:"That night at 8:59 Rodrigo is outside the bathroom door with a towel. Behind him, on the low table in the living room, a phone is buzzing its way slowly towards the edge."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"rodrigo", ja:"トビーさん、[電話]{でんわ}ですよ。", en:"Toby, your phone's ringing."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Toby looks at the screen. It says *Home*. It is nearly ten at night where home is, which is late for a farm."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"toby", ja:"あ、だいじょうぶです。[後]{あと}でかけます。", en:"Oh, it's fine. I'll call back later.", gl:"だいじょうぶ: fine, all right. 電話をかける: to make a phone call."},
    {t:"narr", text:"He turns the phone face down and smiles, the same easy smile he has for everything. The buzzing stops. At 9:19 Rodrigo comes out of the bath, having sung, by his standards, in a whisper. The phone is still face down on the table. Toby has gone up the stairs, sideways, without it."},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u3-x1", type:"mcq", q:"Mrs Satō says このかいだんはあぶないですから、[走]{はし}らないでください. What is she asking Rodrigo to do?", options:[
      {t:"Not to run on the stairs, because they are dangerous", ok:true, why:"Right. ～ないでください is \"please don't\", and から gives her reason: あぶないですから, because they are dangerous."},
      {t:"To run, because he is late", why:"[走]{はし}ってください would be \"please run\". She says [走]{はし}らないでください, with the ない-form: please don't."},
      {t:"Not to use the stairs at all", why:"She only rules out running ([走]{はし}る). Toby uses the stairs a moment earlier, slowly and sideways, and nobody objects."},
      {t:"To be quiet on the stairs", why:"The quiet was for the bath: [小]{ちい}さい[声]{こえ}で[歌]{うた}ってください. On the stairs the problem is speed."}]}},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u3-x2", type:"mcq", q:"Which of these is against the rules at Kamome House?", options:[
      {t:"おふろでねます。", ok:true, why:"Right. The line in red says おふろでねてはいけません: you must not sleep in the bath. Toby has managed it [二回]{にかい}."},
      {t:"おふろで[小]{ちい}さい[声]{こえ}で[歌]{うた}います。", why:"That one is allowed. Rodrigo asked [歌]{うた}ってもいいですか, and Mrs Satō answered [小]{ちい}さい[声]{こえ}で[歌]{うた}ってください."},
      {t:"[朝]{あさ}、シャワーをつかいます。", why:"That's fine: [朝]{あさ}はシャワーだけです. It is the morning bath that isn't on the timetable."},
      {t:"[黒]{くろ}いインクで[書]{か}きます。", why:"That was at the city office, and Mrs Satō said [書]{か}いてもいいです: you may."}]}},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u3-x3", type:"type", q:"Rodrigo answers Mrs Satō with わかった. Type the polite form she asks for instead, in hiragana.", book:"Write the polite (ます) past form of わかる in hiragana.", answer:"わかりました",
      hint:"わかった is a plain past form, so you need the polite past: ～ました.",
      wrongs:[{v:"わかります", why:"That is polite, but it is the present. わかった is past, so the polite form is past too: わかりました."},{v:"わかった", why:"That is the plain form Rodrigo used. Mrs Satō wants the ます version: わかりました."}],
      why:"わかりました: the polite past of わかる. It means the same as わかった; it is simply the one you say to a landlady."}},
    {t:"lang", items:["～てもいいですか asks permission. Rodrigo uses it three times: [入]{はい}ってもいいですか, [歌]{うた}ってもいいですか, [書]{か}いてもいいですか. Only the last gets a plain yes: [書]{か}いてもいいです.", "A rule and a request: the door says おふろでねてはいけません (*you must not*), which is a rule for everyone. Mrs Satō says [走]{はし}らないでください (*please don't*), which is a request to one person.", "Counters: [一人]{ひとり}[二十分]{にじゅっぷん}, [二回]{にかい}, [四十七番]{よんじゅうななばん}, もう[一枚]{いちまい}. People, minutes, times, queue numbers and sheets of paper each have their own counting word."]},
    {t:"reflect", q:"Mrs Satō corrects Rodrigo once and then trusts him to remember. When someone corrects your Japanese, what makes the correction easy to take?"}
  ]},
  {unit:"e3u4", n:4, title:"The noticeboard", month:"May", level:"N5", parts:[
    {t:"narr", text:"May. The noticeboard by the front door is where Kamome House keeps its public life: the rubbish calendar, a cooking rota, and Mrs Satō's pencil tally of what the cat is called, which this week stands at nine. This morning there is something new, pinned dead centre with four pins."},
    {t:"plates", title:"The notice", hint:"Read each line of the notice, then tap it to check.", items:[
      {ja:"なりはま クリーンデー", ro:"Nari-hama kurīn dē", who:"Nari-hama Clean-up Day. Nari-hama, the *ringing beach*, is the stretch of sand outside the harbour. It squeaks under your feet, but only when it is very clean, so every May the whole town turns out to clean it."},
      {ja:"五月十七日（日）", ro:"ごがつ じゅうしちにち（にち）", who:"17 May, a Sunday. The kanji in brackets is the first kanji of 日よう日 (*nichiyōbi*)."},
      {ja:"午前八時から十時まで", ro:"ごぜん はちじ から じゅうじ まで", who:"From 8 to 10 in the morning. 午前 is a.m.; p.m. would be 午後."},
      {ja:"雨の日は休みです", ro:"あめの ひは やすみです", who:"*If it rains, it's off.* 雨 (rain) and 休 (rest) are both N5 kanji."},
      {ja:"七人で行きましょう！", ro:"しちにんで いきましょう", who:"*Let's all seven of us go!* Added at the bottom in Mrs Satō's pencil. It is not a suggestion."}]},
    {t:"narr", text:"Mrs Satō is still holding the box of pins. The buckets and tongs for the beach live in the downstairs storeroom, along with everything the Satō family has owned since the 1970s. She has picked her volunteers in the usual way, by seeing who came down the stairs first."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"fumiko", ja:"どうぐはものおきの[中]{なか}にあります。トビーさん、あおいさん、お[願]{ねが}いします。", en:"The equipment is in the storeroom. Toby, Aoi, if you would.", gl:"どうぐ: tools, equipment. ものおき: a storeroom."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"aoi", ja:"ものおきのどこですか。", en:"Where in the storeroom?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"fumiko", ja:"…[中]{なか}です。", en:"...Inside."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Toby has known this house since he was fifteen, when a school exchange gave him three weeks with the Satōs. Aoi came in April from Saitama, by way of a university in Tokyo, and has not unpacked all her boxes. Toby is polite to everyone, furniture included. Aoi thinks nobody is that polite by accident. Toby thinks Aoi is a little cold. Each has been too polite to say so."},
    {t:"narr", text:"The storeroom is the biggest room in the house, and the fullest: fifty years of one family, in boxes, every box labelled in the same firm teacher's hand."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"toby", ja:"[上]{うえ}のはこは「[本]{ほん}」です。", en:"The top box says \"Books\".", gl:"はこ: a box."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"aoi", ja:"[下]{した}のはこは？", en:"And the one under it?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"toby", ja:"「[古]{ふる}い[本]{ほん}」です。", en:"\"Old books\"."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"aoi", ja:"その[右]{みぎ}は？", en:"And to the right of that?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"toby", ja:"…「もっと[古]{ふる}い[本]{ほん}」です。", en:"...\"Older books\".", gl:"もっと: more."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Toby lifts each box down as if it might be asleep. When he bumps one, he apologises to it. Aoi adds this to her evidence."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"aoi", ja:"トビーさん、[時間]{じかん}がありません。[大]{おお}きいはこは[外]{そと}に[出]{だ}してください。", en:"Toby, we haven't got time. Put the big boxes outside, please."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"toby", ja:"この[小]{ちい}さいはこは？「すてないでください」です。", en:"What about this small one? It says \"Please do not throw away\".", gl:"すてる: to throw away."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"aoi", ja:"[中]{なか}は[何]{なん}ですか。", en:"What's in it?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"toby", ja:"…[古]{ふる}いラジオです。[三]{みっ}つあります。", en:"...Old radios. Three of them."},
    {t:"narr", text:"That label is in a different hand, an engineer's capitals. Mr Satō mends things. The radios go back exactly where they were."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"toby", ja:"あおいさんは、なりはまへ[行]{い}きましたか。", en:"Have you been to Nari-hama, Aoi?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"aoi", ja:"…いいえ。[時間]{じかん}がありませんから。", en:"...No. I haven't had the time."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Aoi says she is only in Shioura for two years, and a beach is a beach. There is sand in the turn-ups of her jeans. Toby, being polite, doesn't see it."},
    {t:"line", mood:"yay", who:"aoi", ja:"あ、ありました。バケツが[三]{みっ}つ、トングが[七本]{ななほん}。", en:"Ah, found them. Three buckets, seven pairs of tongs.", gl:"バケツ: a bucket. トング: tongs."},
    {t:"narr", text:"The equipment is at the very back, as promised: inside. Behind the buckets, on the lowest shelf, pushed to the wall where nobody puts a thing they mean to find again, there is a biscuit tin. The cat, who has supervised all morning from the top of the older books, comes down and sits beside it."},
    {t:"cat", pose:"curious", alt:"The cat sitting beside the biscuit tin, ears forward"},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"toby", ja:"センセイ、それは[何]{なん}ですか。", en:"Sensei, what's that?", gl:"センセイ: *Teacher*, which is Toby's name for the cat. He says she taught him the back lanes."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"aoi", ja:"…ねこに[聞]{き}いていますか。", en:"...Are you asking the cat?"},
    {t:"narr", text:"Aoi does not name strays. She opens the tin. Envelopes, a great many of them, thin blue airmail paper with red and navy stripes round the edges, tied in bundles with kitchen string. The stamps are Australian. Toby, who is also Australian, goes very still."},
    {t:"plates", title:"In the tin", hint:"Three things are written in Japanese. Read each one, then tap to check.", items:[
      {ja:"文子", ro:"ふみこ", who:"Inside the lid, in a schoolgirl's brush pen: *Fumiko*. 文 means writing or letters, and 子 (child) ends a great many girls' names of her generation. Mrs Satō's given name is Fumiko."},
      {ja:"汐浦市 川南 126", ro:"しおうらし かわみなみ 126", who:"The address on the front of every envelope: 126 Kawaminami, Shioura. 川 is river and 南 is south. Neither of them has ever seen it on a street sign in Shioura."},
      {ja:"一九六八年 二月 三日", ro:"せんきゅうひゃくろくじゅうはちねん にがつ みっか", who:"3 February 1968, pencilled on the back of the top envelope, perhaps the day it arrived. Every envelope has a date like it. This is the latest one in the tin."}]},
    {t:"note", text:"Look at how a kanji was written and you learn something about who wrote it. These addresses were copied stroke by careful stroke, in the wrong order, the way you would copy a drawing. Somebody far away, who couldn't read them, got every one of them right."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"toby", ja:"[一九六八年]{せんきゅうひゃくろくじゅうはちねん}の[二月]{にがつ}…。", en:"February 1968..."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"aoi", ja:"[五十八年前]{ごじゅうはちねんまえ}です。[読]{よ}みたいです。", en:"Fifty-eight years ago. I want to read them."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"toby", ja:"[読]{よ}んではいけません。さとうさんのてがみですから。", en:"We mustn't. They're Mrs Satō's letters.", gl:"てがみ: a letter."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"aoi", ja:"[中]{なか}は[読]{よ}みません。[外]{そと}だけです。", en:"I won't read the insides. Only the outsides."},
    {t:"narr", text:"It is the first thing they have agreed on all morning, and it takes them through every bundle: the same address in the same careful kanji, the dates climbing from 1963 to 1968 and then stopping. They are still kneeling there when the light from the doorway changes."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"fumiko", ja:"…それは[私]{わたし}のです。", en:"...That's mine."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Mrs Satō takes the tin in both hands. She doesn't open it, and she doesn't say what it is. For once she has no correction to make at all."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"fumiko", ja:"バケツは[三]{みっ}つありましたか。", en:"Were there three buckets?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"toby", ja:"はい、[三]{みっ}つありました。", en:"Yes. Three."},
    {t:"narr", text:"She nods, and carries the tin across the garden to the cottage herself. Aoi, who has a question, doesn't ask it. Toby, who would normally apologise, doesn't do that either."},
    {t:"narr", text:"By evening two names on the notice have been ticked off in pencil. The cat tally has not moved all day."},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u4-x1", type:"mcq", q:"The notice says 五月十七日（日）午前八時から十時まで. When is the clean-up?", options:[
      {t:"Sunday 17 May, 8 to 10 in the morning", ok:true, why:"Right. 五月 is May, 十七日 is the 17th, （日） is Sunday, and 午前 puts 八時から十時まで in the morning."},
      {t:"Sunday 17 May, 8 to 10 in the evening", why:"The evening would be 午後. The notice says 午前: before noon."},
      {t:"Monday 17 May, 8 to 10 in the morning", why:"Monday is （月）. The kanji in the brackets is 日, for 日よう日, Sunday."},
      {t:"Sunday 7 May, 8 to 10 in the morning", why:"七日 would be the 7th. The notice says 十七日: ten and seven, the 17th."}]}},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u4-x2", type:"mcq", q:"The latest date in the tin is 一九六八年二月三日. Which date is that?", options:[
      {t:"3 February 1968", ok:true, why:"Right. 一九六八年 gives the year one digit at a time, 二月 is February, and 三日 (みっか) is the 3rd."},
      {t:"2 March 1968", why:"Japanese dates run from big to small: year, then month (月), then day (日). 二月三日 is month 2, day 3."},
      {t:"3 February 1986", why:"Read the digits in order: 一・九・六・八. Six comes before eight, so it is 1968."},
      {t:"3 February 1698", why:"Read the digits in order: 一・九・六・八. Nine comes before six, so it is 1968."}]}},
    {t:"lang", items:["One kanji, three readings: 日 is にち in 十七日, ひ in 雨の日, and か in 三日 (みっか). The word around it tells you which.", "Position kanji do the pointing in the storeroom: [上]{うえ}のはこ, [下]{した}のはこ, その[右]{みぎ}, ものおきの[中]{なか}, [外]{そと}に[出]{だ}してください.", "A year can be written digit by digit, as in 一九六八年, but it is read as an ordinary number: せんきゅうひゃくろくじゅうはちねん."]},
    {t:"reflect", q:"Toby and Aoi agree to read only the outsides of the envelopes. Where would you have drawn the line?"}
  ]},
  {unit:"e3u5", n:5, title:"Kitchen talk", month:"June", level:"N4", parts:[
    {t:"narr", text:"*Previously at Kamome House:* Mrs Satō taught Rodrigo, once, that わかった is for friends and わかりました is for landladies. Toby and Aoi found a tin of old airmail letters in the storeroom, and Mrs Satō carried it away without a word."},
    {t:"narr", text:"A Thursday in June, half past five, and it has been raining since Monday. The kitchen at Kamome House has one stove with two rings, and one of the rings has opinions. Kaito is at the good one, filling the big pot. Rodrigo arrives in the doorway holding a cabbage."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"kaito", ja:"あの…今日はぼくの[番]{ばん}ですけど。", en:"Um... it's my turn today, actually.", gl:"番 (ばん): a turn. ～けど: \"but…\", left hanging to soften what you say."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"rodrigo", ja:"え？今日はぼくの[番]{ばん}ですよ。チェスカさんが「[木曜日]{もくようび}、お[願]{ねが}い」と言いました。", en:"What? It's my turn today. Cheska said, \"Thursday, please.\""},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"kaito", ja:"…ぼくにも言いました。グループチャットで。", en:"...She said it to me too. In the group chat."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Cheska trades away every cooking turn she is given, at a fair rate of two cleaning turns each. She has never before sold the same Thursday twice. Rodrigo doesn't read the house chat, which moves faster than his kanji. Kaito doesn't speak at breakfast."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"rodrigo", ja:"かいと、もう[二]{に}か[月]{げつ}だよ。「です・ます」はいらない。[友]{とも}だちだから。", en:"Kaito, it's been two months. We don't need desu and masu. We're friends."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"kaito", ja:"…いいんですか。", en:"...Is that really OK?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"yay", who:"rodrigo", ja:"いいんだ！", en:"It is!"},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"kaito", ja:"…うん。じゃあ、今日、おれの[番]{ばん}。", en:"...OK. Then today's my turn.", gl:"おれ: a rough, casual \"I\" that men use with friends. ぼく is the softer one."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Kaito's casual Japanese is the kind you type with one thumb: no particles, and nothing left in that could be left out. Rodrigo's is what it was on his first day, before Mrs Satō and the stairs. He learned it from heroes."},
    {t:"line", mood:"yay", who:"rodrigo", ja:"ちがう！今日はおれの[番]{ばん}だ！このキャベツを見ろ！", en:"Wrong! Today is my turn! Behold this cabbage!", gl:"見ろ: \"Look!\", the blunt command form of 見る. Anime heroes use it constantly; housemates almost never do."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"kaito", ja:"見てる。キャベツだね。", en:"I'm looking. It's a cabbage."},
    {t:"line", mood:"yay", who:"rodrigo", ja:"これで[七人]{しちにん}のばんごはんを[作]{つく}る！", en:"With this I shall make dinner for seven!", gl:"ばんごはん: dinner."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"kaito", ja:"…キャベツ[一]{ひと}つで？", en:"...With one cabbage?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"rodrigo", ja:"…たまごもある。", en:"...There are eggs too."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Kaito grew up in his family's soba shop and can cost a dinner at a glance. This one comes to about two hundred yen for seven people. He looks at the cabbage, then at Rodrigo, and says nothing. Saying nothing is Kaito's first language."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"kaito", ja:"…おれ、そば[作]{つく}りたいんだけど。", en:"...Thing is, I want to make soba.", gl:"そば: buckwheat noodles. ～んだけど: \"the thing is…\", trailing off."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"rodrigo", ja:"だめだ！チェスカに「おれが[作]{つく}る」と言った。やくそくはやくそくだ！", en:"No! I told Cheska, \"I'll cook.\" A promise is a promise!", gl:"やくそく: a promise."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"kaito", ja:"おれも言ったよ。「やる」って。", en:"I said it too. \"I'll do it.\"", gl:"やる: to do (casual). って: the casual と for quoting."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Stalemate. The pot comes to the boil with nothing in it. Then the door opens on Yến, straight from the lab, holding a tub of something that needs to be cold."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"yen", ja:"お[疲]{つか}れさまです。お[話]{はな}し[中]{ちゅう}、[失礼]{しつれい}いたします。[冷蔵庫]{れいぞうこ}を[使]{つか}ってもよろしいでしょうか。", en:"Good evening, both. I do apologise for interrupting. Might I possibly use the refrigerator?", gl:"お疲れさまです: the greeting colleagues give each other at work. 失礼いたします: \"excuse me\", very formal. 冷蔵庫 (れいぞうこ): fridge. よろしいでしょうか: a very polite いいですか."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"kaito", ja:"…どうぞ。", en:"...Go ahead."},
    {t:"line", mood:"yay", who:"rodrigo", ja:"もちろんだ！", en:"But of course!"},
    {t:"narr", text:"Mrs Satō has come in out of the rain behind her, with a parcel wrapped in newspaper. She has heard all three of them: the hero, the thumb, the board meeting. She corrects exactly one."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"fumiko", ja:"イエンさん、ここは[会社]{かいしゃ}じゃありませんよ。うちです。「[冷蔵庫]{れいぞうこ}、[使]{つか}うね」でいいんです。", en:"Yến, this isn't a company. It's home. \"Using the fridge, OK?\" is all you need.", gl:"うち: home, our place. ～でいい: ～ is fine, ～ is enough."},
    {t:"note", text:"Polite is a distance, and more of it isn't always better. In April Mrs Satō moved Rodrigo a step further from his landlady. In June she moves Yến a step closer to her housemates. It is the same lesson both times: say it the way the room says it. Rodrigo's おれの番だ she lets pass. He is talking to a friend, in a kitchen."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"yen", ja:"…[冷蔵庫]{れいぞうこ}、[使]{つか}う…ね。", en:"...Using the fridge... OK?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"kaito", ja:"うん。", en:"Yeah."},
    {t:"narr", text:"It costs Yến more than a client presentation, and it is the first casual sentence she has said in this house. Kaito answers as if she had been saying it for years, which is the kindest thing available. Then Mrs Satō unwraps the newspaper."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"fumiko", ja:"[港]{みなと}であじが[安]{やす}かったんです。[七匹]{ななひき}で[五百円]{ごひゃくえん}。だれが[料理]{りょうり}しますか。", en:"The horse mackerel was cheap at the harbour, you see. Seven for five hundred yen. Who's cooking?", gl:"港 (みなと): harbour. あじ: horse mackerel, a small silver fish."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Seven fish, whole, look up at Rodrigo. He has met this look before, in a bowl of squid."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"rodrigo", ja:"…これ、どうやって[切]{き}るんだ？", en:"...How do you cut one of these?", gl:"どうやって: how, in what way."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"kaito", ja:"おれが[切]{き}る。ロドリゴはキャベツ[切]{き}って。ごはんも。", en:"I'll do the fish. You cut the cabbage. And do the rice.", gl:"切って: the て-form on its own is a casual request, a short ～てください."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"rodrigo", ja:"じゃあ、今日はだれの[番]{ばん}だ？", en:"Then whose turn is it today?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"kaito", ja:"…[二人]{ふたり}の[番]{ばん}。", en:"...Both of ours."},
    {t:"line", mood:"yay", who:"rodrigo", ja:"[二人]{ふたり}の[番]{ばん}か！よし、行くぞ、かいと！", en:"Both of ours! Right. Here we go, Kaito!", gl:"ぞ: a rough, hero-ish よ."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"kaito", ja:"…[台所]{だいどころ}だよ、ここ。", en:"...It's a kitchen, this.", gl:"台所 (だいどころ): kitchen."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Kaito cleans seven fish in the time it takes Rodrigo to quarter one cabbage. Nobody mentions how far a cabbage was going to go. Before long there is a black-and-white face at the window, watching the knife."},
    {t:"cat", pose:"smug", alt:"The cat at the kitchen window"},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"kaito", ja:"ししょう、まだだよ。", en:"Not yet, Master.", gl:"ししょう (師匠): the master of a craft. It is Kaito's name for the cat, who supervises his cooking."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"fumiko", ja:"…ししょう？", en:"...Master?"},
    {t:"narr", text:"Mrs Satō goes out to the hall, where the pencil is. At dinner Cheska eats two fish, quietly, and asks who cooked. She gets the same word from both ends of the table: おれ."},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u5-x1", type:"mcq", q:"Why do Kaito and Rodrigo both think Thursday is their turn to cook?", options:[
      {t:"Cheska asked both of them", ok:true, why:"Right. Rodrigo says チェスカさんが「[木曜日]{もくようび}、お[願]{ねが}い」と言いました, and Kaito answers ぼくにも言いました: she said it to me too."},
      {t:"Mrs Satō asked both of them", why:"Mrs Satō only arrives later, with the fish. It was Cheska: チェスカさんが…と言いました."},
      {t:"Rodrigo read the group chat wrong", why:"Rodrigo doesn't read the group chat at all. Cheska asked him in person, and asked Kaito グループチャットで."},
      {t:"Kaito wants to cook every day", why:"Kaito only says he wants to make soba today: そば[作]{つく}りたいんだけど."}]}},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u5-x2", type:"mcq", q:"Kaito says 見てる。キャベツだね。 What is 見てる short for?", options:[
      {t:"見ている", ok:true, why:"Right. In casual speech ～ている loses its い: 見ている → 見てる. *I'm looking.*"},
      {t:"見ていた", why:"That is the past, *was looking*. Its casual form is 見てた."},
      {t:"見てください", why:"A casual request is the て-form alone, like Kaito's キャベツ[切]{き}って. 見てる has る on the end: it is ～ている."},
      {t:"見ます", why:"見ます is the polite form of 見る, *look* or *will look*. 見てる is the casual form of 見ている, *am looking*."}]}},
    {t:"lang", items:["The switch: Kaito opens politely (ぼくの[番]{ばん}ですけど) and only changes when the older Rodrigo offers: 「です・ます」はいらない. He checks first (いいんですか), then drops everything at once: 今日、おれの[番]{ばん}.", "Quoting: Rodrigo quotes with と (「おれが[作]{つく}る」と言った), and Kaito with casual って after the quote (「やる」って). Both mean *said that…*", "～んです explains: Mrs Satō's あじが[安]{やす}かったんです gives the reason she is standing there with seven fish, and Kaito's いいんですか asks for an explanation before he dares to switch."]},
    {t:"reflect", q:"Rodrigo tells Kaito 「です・ます」はいらない. In your own language, how do you know when you can drop the formality with someone, and who usually says so first?"}
  ]},
  {unit:"e3u6", n:6, title:"The house app", month:"June", level:"N4", parts:[
    {t:"narr", text:"*Previously at Kamome House:* Cheska promised one Thursday to two cooks. Kaito and Rodrigo ended up sharing the stove, and Mrs Satō told Yến that a kitchen is not a company."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Kaito does not like a system that can promise one Thursday twice. He came home from his night shift on Friday and did not go to bed. By Saturday lunchtime there was a square code pinned to the noticeboard, under the cat tally, and the house had an app: who cooks, who cleans, whose bath it is, which rubbish goes out tomorrow, and a button marked かわる, *swap*."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Everyone installed it except Mr Satō, who has no smartphone and considers the barometer sufficient. Mrs Satō installed it first. She has since left four sticky notes on the board, each beginning *I noticed*."},
    {t:"narr", text:"A week later, before dinner, Yến sits down beside Kaito at the low table. Since the Thursday of the fish she has been practising plain speech on him, as the person least likely to comment."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"yen", ja:"かいと、このアプリ、[一人]{ひとり}で[作]{つく}った？", en:"Kaito, did you make this app on your own?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"kaito", ja:"…うん。[一晩]{ひとばん}で。", en:"...Yeah. In a night.", gl:"一晩 (ひとばん): one night."},
    {t:"line", mood:"yay", who:"yen", ja:"[一晩]{ひとばん}で[作]{つく}れるんだ。すごいね。", en:"You can build this in one night. That's impressive."},
    {t:"narr", text:"From Yến this is a great deal, and it would have been a good place to stop. But she spent four years building software for clients, and in that world nothing ships that only one person has read."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"yen", ja:"コード、見せてくれない？レビューしてあげる。", en:"Would you show me the code? I'll review it for you.", gl:"コード: code. レビュー: a review. In a code review, another programmer reads your code before it is used."},
    {t:"note", text:"～てあげる is a generous verb with a sting in it. It says *I am doing you a favour*, which is fine for carrying a friend's shopping and less fine for an offer to judge somebody's work. Yến means it kindly. Kaito hears the favour."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"kaito", ja:"…まだ見せられない。", en:"...I can't show you yet."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"yen", ja:"どうして？", en:"Why not?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"kaito", ja:"まだ、きれいじゃないから。きれいになったら、見せる。", en:"It's not clean yet. When it's clean, I'll show you."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"yen", ja:"きれいじゃなくてもいいよ。レビューすれば、きれいになるから。", en:"It doesn't have to be clean. If we review it, it gets clean."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"kaito", ja:"ちゃんと[動]{うご}いてるよ。みんな[使]{つか}える。", en:"It works fine. Everyone can use it.", gl:"ちゃんと: properly. 動く (うごく): to move; of a machine or a program, to work."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"yen", ja:"[動]{うご}くだけじゃだめ。テストは書いた？", en:"Working isn't enough. Did you write tests?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"kaito", ja:"…書いてない。", en:"...No."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"yen", ja:"書かなきゃ。バグがあったら、どうするつもり？", en:"You have to. If there's a bug, what do you plan to do?", gl:"バグ: a bug, a mistake in a program."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"kaito", ja:"バグはない。", en:"There are no bugs."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Toby comes in from the vegetable patch behind the cottage with soil on his knees and his phone in his hand. He has the look of a man who has checked something twice."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"toby", ja:"かいとくん、ちょっといい？ぼく、[今週]{こんしゅう}、[四回]{よんかい}[料理]{りょうり}しなければならないんだけど…。", en:"Kaito, have you got a second? It says I have to cook four times this week...", gl:"今週 (こんしゅう): this week."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"yen", ja:"[四回]{よんかい}？どうして？", en:"Four times? Why?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"toby", ja:"「かわって」が来ると、「いいよ」をおしてしまうんだ。", en:"Whenever a swap request comes, I end up pressing \"OK\".", gl:"かわる: to swap, to take someone's place. おす: to press."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Toby has never refused anybody anything, in either of his languages. The app has made saying yes a single tap."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"yen", ja:"ほら、バグだよ。[一人]{ひとり}が[何回]{なんかい}でもかわれる。", en:"There, see? A bug. One person can swap any number of times.", gl:"ほら: \"see?\", \"look\". 何回でも: any number of times."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"kaito", ja:"バグじゃない。トビーが「いいよ」をおさなければ、いいんだよ。", en:"It's not a bug. It's fine as long as Toby doesn't press \"OK\"."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"toby", ja:"…それはそうだね。ごめん。", en:"...Well, that's true. Sorry.", gl:"ごめん: sorry (casual)."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"yen", ja:"[人]{ひと}はおしてしまうの。だから、「かわるのは[一週間]{いっしゅうかん}に[二回]{にかい}まで」というルールを[入]{い}れなければならない。", en:"People do press it. So you have to put in a rule: no more than two swaps a week.", gl:"～の at the end: a soft, explaining ～んだ. ～というルール: a rule that says ～."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"kaito", ja:"…おれのアプリだよ。", en:"...It's my app."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"yen", ja:"みんなのアプリだよ。[仕事]{しごと}なら、レビューしていないコードは[出]{だ}せない。", en:"It's everyone's app. If this were work, you couldn't release code nobody has reviewed.", gl:"仕事 (しごと): work, a job. 出す: here, to release."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"kaito", ja:"[仕事]{しごと}じゃない。…バイト、行かなきゃ。", en:"It isn't work. ...I've got to get to my shift.", gl:"バイト: a part-time job."},
    {t:"narr", text:"He closes the laptop without a sound. Even Kaito's exits are quiet. Everything Yến said was correct. She sits and looks at the place where the laptop was."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"toby", ja:"ぼくは[四回]{よんかい}[作]{つく}ってもいいよ。ほんとに。", en:"I don't mind cooking four times. Really.", gl:"ほんとに: really."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"yen", ja:"…それがバグなんだよ、トビー。", en:"...That is the bug, Toby."},
    {t:"narr", text:"So Toby cooks. At dinner Kaito's place is empty, and Cheska is quiet in a way that isn't her usual quiet. She has not traded away a single cooking turn all week. Beside her bowl is a sheet of paper, folded down to one square."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"toby", ja:"チェスカ、それ、[何]{なん}の[地図]{ちず}？", en:"Cheska, what's that a map of?", gl:"地図 (ちず): a map."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"cheska", ja:"ううん、[何]{なん}でもない。[後]{あと}で読もうと[思]{おも}って。", en:"Oh, it's nothing. I thought I'd read it later.", gl:"何でもない: it's nothing."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"cheska", ja:"食べよう。さめちゃうよ。", en:"Let's eat. It'll get cold.", gl:"さめる: to go cold."},
    {t:"narr", text:"She has read it already, three times, on her own. It is the city's hazard map. The square she has left showing is the old district by the river, with this street on it, and the square is not white. Toby knows that kind of *nothing*. He uses it himself. He passes her the rice."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Two in the morning. Kaito is on his break behind the convenience store. Yến is upstairs with a record on, very low, not working. Her phone lights up."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"kaito", ja:"[起]{お}きてる？", en:"You awake?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"yen", ja:"[起]{お}きてる。", en:"I'm awake."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"kaito", ja:"コード、[送]{おく}っておいた。見てもいいよ。でも、[笑]{わら}わないで。", en:"I've sent you the code. You can look. But don't laugh.", gl:"送る (おくる): to send. 笑う (わらう): to laugh."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"yen", ja:"[笑]{わら}わないよ。…「してあげる」はよくなかった。ごめん。", en:"I won't laugh. ...\"I'll do it for you\" wasn't right. Sorry."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"yen", ja:"[明日]{あした}、いっしょに見よう。", en:"Let's look at it together tomorrow."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"kaito", ja:"…うん。トビーのバグ、[直]{なお}しておく。", en:"...OK. I'll fix the Toby bug before then.", gl:"直す (なおす): to fix."},
    {t:"narr", text:"He has called it a bug. From Kaito that is very nearly an apology. Downstairs one more light is still on, in Room 101, where on other nights at this hour there would be the small sounds of an old horror film. Tonight there is only a map, unfolded all the way, on the floor."},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u6-x1", type:"mcq", q:"Kaito says まだ見せられない. What does he mean?", options:[
      {t:"He can't show the code yet", ok:true, why:"Right. 見せられない is the potential form of 見せる in the negative: *can't show*. His reason follows: まだ、きれいじゃないから."},
      {t:"He hasn't looked at the code yet", why:"That would be まだ見ていない. 見せる is *show*, not *look*, and ～られない here means *can't*."},
      {t:"He doesn't have to show the code", why:"*Doesn't have to* is ～なくてもいい: 見せなくてもいい. 見せられない is *can't show*."},
      {t:"He must not show the code", why:"*Must not* is ～てはいけない: 見せてはいけない. 見せられない is *can't show*."}]}},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u6-x2", type:"mcq", q:"At two in the morning Kaito writes トビーのバグ、[直]{なお}しておく. What is he promising?", options:[
      {t:"To fix the swap problem in advance, before he and Yến look at the code tomorrow", ok:true, why:"Right. ～ておく is doing something now so that it is ready for later, and [直]{なお}す is *fix*. For the first time he calls it a バグ."},
      {t:"That he has already fixed it", why:"*Already fixed* would be [直]{なお}しておいた, in the past, like his [送]{おく}っておいた. [直]{なお}しておく is still to come."},
      {t:"To make Toby fix it", why:"There is nobody else in the sentence. トビーのバグ is only what Kaito calls the problem: the bug Toby found by saying yes to everyone."},
      {t:"To leave the problem as it is", why:"～ておく can mean leaving something as it is, but not with [直]{なお}す: you can't fix a thing and leave it alone."}]}},
    {t:"lang", items:["Can and can't: [一晩]{ひとばん}で[作]{つく}れる, みんな[使]{つか}える, 見せられない, [出]{だ}せない. The potential form carries most of the argument: what Kaito can do alone, and what Yến says nobody can.", "Favours: 見せてくれない？ asks Kaito to do something for her, and that is fine. レビューしてあげる offers to do something for him, and from someone more experienced it can sound as if she is doing him a kindness he didn't ask for. She takes it back herself: 「してあげる」はよくなかった.", "Must, and don't have to: 書かなきゃ and [入]{い}れなければならない are the same *must*, casual and formal. きれいじゃなくてもいい is the opposite: it doesn't have to be."]},
    {t:"reflect", q:"Yến is right about the code, and Kaito still closes the laptop. Think of a time someone was right about your work. What made it easier, or harder, to hear?"}
  ]},
  {unit:"e3u7", n:7, title:"The last festival?", month:"July–August", level:"N4", parts:[
    {t:"narr", text:"*Previously at Kamome House:* Kaito built the house a chore app in one night, and at two in the morning he finally let Yến read the code. The app also proved that Toby says yes to everything he is asked."},
    {t:"narr", text:"The last week of July. Tsubame-dōri, Swallow Street, is the covered shopping street two blocks from the house, and about every second shutter on it is down for good. Halfway along is a tea shop older than the roof. It belongs to Hamada Chiyo, who is past eighty, has had a weak left hand since a small stroke last year, and is Aoi's grandmother. Last month she ordered a festival poster from the artist in Room 102."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"chiyo", ja:"いらっしゃいませ。…あら、ロドリゴさん。", en:"Welcome. ...Oh, it's you, Rodrigo.", gl:"いらっしゃいませ: what shop staff say when you walk in. It comes from いらっしゃる, the respectful verb for *come*."},
    {t:"line", mood:"yay", who:"rodrigo", ja:"ちよさん！ポスターができました！", en:"Chiyo-san! The poster is finished!"},
    {t:"narr", text:"He unrolls it across the counter. Fountain pen, three inks: the arcade roof, the paper lanterns, and seven swallows going under them at speed. On the step of a tea shop sits a black-and-white cat."},
    {t:"plates", title:"The poster", hint:"Read each line of the poster, then tap it to check.", items:[
      {ja:"つばめ通り 夏まつり", ro:"つばめどおり なつまつり", who:"The Swallow Street Summer Festival. 通り is a street and 夏 is summer. Rodrigo left つばめ in hiragana: its kanji, 燕, has sixteen strokes, and he wanted the poster readable from a moving bus."},
      {ja:"八月一日（土）", ro:"はちがつ ついたち（ど）", who:"Saturday 1 August. The first of the month has a word of its own, ついたち."},
      {ja:"午後四時から九時まで", ro:"ごご よじ から くじ まで", who:"From 4 to 9 in the evening."},
      {ja:"雨の日も やります", ro:"あめの ひも やります", who:"*On even if it rains.* The beach clean-up in May said 雨の日は休みです. Swallow Street has a roof, and says も."},
      {ja:"英語の あんない あります", ro:"えいごの あんない あります", who:"*English guides available.* あんない (案内) is showing people the way. This line was not in Rodrigo's sketch. The shopkeepers' association added it, and then went looking for some guides."}]},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"chiyo", ja:"…このねこは？", en:"...And this cat?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"yay", who:"rodrigo", ja:"ミチです！", en:"That's Michi!"},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"chiyo", ja:"「ミチ」じゃありませんよ。この[通]{とお}りでは「まっちゃ」と[呼]{よ}ばれています。", en:"She isn't Michi. On this street she is called Matcha.", gl:"まっちゃ (抹茶): powdered green tea. 呼ばれる (よばれる): to be called, the passive of 呼ぶ."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"rodrigo", ja:"[白]{しろ}と[黒]{くろ}なのに、まっちゃですか。", en:"She's black and white, and she's Matcha?", gl:"～のに: even though."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"chiyo", ja:"お[茶]{ちゃ}の[店]{みせ}の[前]{まえ}にいますから。", en:"She sits outside a tea shop."},
    {t:"narr", text:"On this street, that settles it. Chiyo counts the swallows twice and doesn't say why. Then she takes an envelope from under the till."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"chiyo", ja:"はい、これ。ポスターのお金です。", en:"Here you are. For the poster."},
    {t:"line", mood:"yay", who:"rodrigo", ja:"お金はいりません！かきたかったから、かきました！", en:"I need no money! I drew it because I wanted to!"},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"chiyo", ja:"だめですよ。[人]{ひと}に[仕事]{しごと}をさせて、お金を[払]{はら}わない[店]{みせ}は、[長]{なが}く[続]{つづ}きません。", en:"That won't do. A shop that makes people work and doesn't pay them doesn't last long.", gl:"させる: to make someone do, the causative of する. 払う (はらう): to pay. 続く (つづく): to last, to go on."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Hers has lasted sixty years, so he takes her word for it, and the envelope, in both hands. It is the first money anyone in Japan has paid him to draw."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"rodrigo", ja:"…ありがとうございます。", en:"...Thank you."},
    {t:"narr", text:"From Rodrigo that is very quiet indeed. He has one more question, the one the whole street is asking."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"rodrigo", ja:"ちよさん、まつりは今年で[終]{お}わるらしいですね。パン[屋]{や}さんで[聞]{き}きました。", en:"Chiyo-san, I hear this year's festival is going to be the last. They told me at the bakery.", gl:"～らしい: apparently, from what people say. パン屋 (パンや): a bakery."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"chiyo", ja:"[去年]{きょねん}もそう言われましたよ。その[前]{まえ}の[年]{とし}も。", en:"They said that last year too. And the year before."},
    {t:"note", text:"らしい is the grammar of a rumour: it passes on what people are saying without quite saying who. Chiyo answers in the passive, そう言われました, *that was said*, which leaves the speakers out altogether. A whole street can talk like this for years, and does."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Three more shutters have come down since last summer, and the association votes on next year in the autumn. On his way home Rodrigo buys lunch, a proper one, at four in the afternoon."},
    {t:"narr", text:"The first Saturday of August. Within a week the poster was on every shutter in the street, which gave the closed shops something to say for once. Tonight a cruise ship is in the harbour, a first. At a folding table marked ENGLISH sit the two guides the association went looking for. It asked one of them."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"mariya", ja:"ロドリゴのポスター、フェリーのりばにもはってあるんだって。…で、[私]{わたし}、「やる」って言ってないのに、どうしてここにいるの？", en:"Rodrigo's poster is up at the ferry terminal too, I hear. ...So. I never said I'd do this. Why am I sitting here?", gl:"のりば: the place where you board. はる: to stick up. はってある: has been put up, and is still there. ～んだって: \"I hear that…\" (casual)."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"toby", ja:"ちよさんに[頼]{たの}まれて…「[二人]{ふたり}でやります」って言っちゃった。", en:"Chiyo-san asked me, and... I went and said, \"The two of us will do it.\"", gl:"頼む (たのむ): to ask someone to do something. 頼まれる: to be asked. 言っちゃった: casual 言ってしまった."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"mariya", ja:"トビーはいつもそう。[頼]{たの}まれると、[何]{なん}でも「はい」。", en:"You always do this. Somebody asks, and it's yes to anything."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Mariya writes English better than anyone in the house, Toby included. Speaking it is another matter. When a couple in matching sun hats ask where the food is, she turns and looks at Toby. She does the same for the next visitor, and the one after."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"toby", ja:"まりや、[次]{つぎ}は[話]{はな}してみて。", en:"Mariya, you take the next one."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"mariya", ja:"むり。ぜったいまちがえそう。", en:"No way. I just know I'll get it wrong.", gl:"むり: impossible. ぜったい: definitely. まちがえる: to make a mistake. ～そう: looks likely to."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"toby", ja:"まちがえてもいいよ。ぼくも、まちがえながら日本語をおぼえたし。", en:"It's fine to get it wrong. I learned Japanese by getting it wrong as I went.", gl:"おぼえる: to learn, to memorise. ～ながら: while doing."},
    {t:"narr", text:"At ten to seven his phone buzzes twice. He reads it the way he reads all bad news, smiling."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"toby", ja:"…まりや。[七時]{しちじ}に[源]{げん}さんの[屋台]{やたい}を[手伝]{てつだ}うって、[約束]{やくそく}したんだ。", en:"...Mariya. I promised to help at Gen-san's stall at seven.", gl:"屋台 (やたい): a food stall. 手伝う (てつだう): to help. 約束 (やくそく): a promise."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"mariya", ja:"じゃあ、行ってきて。[十分]{じゅっぷん}だけだよ。", en:"Go on, then. Ten minutes, mind."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"toby", ja:"それと…[岩田]{いわた}さんにも。[七時]{しちじ}に。", en:"And... Iwata-san too. At seven."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"mariya", ja:"[二人]{ふたり}に？[同]{おな}じ[時間]{じかん}なのに？", en:"Both of them? For the same time?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"mariya", ja:"あの[二人]{ふたり}、[三十年]{さんじゅうねん}[話]{はな}してないんだよ。[知]{し}ってるでしょ。", en:"Those two haven't spoken to each other in thirty years. You know that."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"toby", ja:"[知]{し}ってる。だから、どっちにも「だめ」と言えなくて…。", en:"I know. That's why I couldn't say no to either of them..."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Gen-san and Mr Iwata are old fishermen, and Toby needs them both for his dialect recordings. Mariya, who took the ferry to school for three years, knows every captain on this coast. She handles it the way a harbourmaster handles two boats and one berth."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"mariya", ja:"[源]{げん}さんが[先]{さき}。[十五分]{じゅうごふん}[手伝]{てつだ}って、それから[岩田]{いわた}さん。「まりやに行かされた」って言っていいから。", en:"Gen-san first. Fifteen minutes there, then Iwata-san. You can tell them Mariya made you go.", gl:"行かされる: to be made to go, the causative-passive of 行く."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"toby", ja:"…ごめん。すぐ[戻]{もど}る。", en:"...Sorry. Back soon.", gl:"戻る (もどる): to come back."},
    {t:"narr", text:"That leaves one guide at the table, and naturally this is when the coach from the cruise ship arrives. A grandmother with a paper fan wants to know what *Tsubame* means. Mariya hears her own voice say: swallow. That sounds wrong, so she adds: the bird, not this, and gulps, a hand at her throat. The grandmother laughs until she needs the fan. Her English is quick and musical and nothing like the listening tests, and Mariya understands all of it. Nobody is marking. They would like some tea. Mariya knows a shop."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"chiyo", ja:"いらっしゃいませ。…まりやちゃん、[英語]{えいご}、じょうずですね。", en:"Welcome. ...Mariya, your English is very good."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"mariya", ja:"ぜんぜんです。でも、[通]{つう}じたみたいです。", en:"Not at all. But it seems to have got through.", gl:"通じる (つうじる): to get through, to be understood. ～みたい: it seems."},
    {t:"narr", text:"By eight the shop has sold more tea than in the whole of July, and a smell of grilled squid comes in ahead of Toby."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"toby", ja:"ただいま…。[源]{げん}さんにイカを[焼]{や}かされて、[岩田]{いわた}さんにビールを[飲]{の}まされた。", en:"I'm back... Gen-san had me grilling squid, and then Iwata-san made me drink beer.", gl:"イカ: squid. 焼く (やく): to grill. 焼かされる, 飲まされる: to be made to grill, to be made to drink."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"mariya", ja:"[楽]{たの}しそうだね。", en:"You look as if you had a lovely time."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"mariya", ja:"今日、[私]{わたし}はトビーに[英語]{えいご}を[話]{はな}させられた。[今度]{こんど}は、[私]{わたし}がトビーに「ノー」と言わせるからね。", en:"Today you made me speak English. Next time, I'm going to make you say no.", gl:"話させられる: to be made to speak. 言わせる: to make someone say. 今度 (こんど): next time."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"toby", ja:"…はい。", en:"...Yes."},
    {t:"narr", text:"It is, of course, a yes. She lets it go, for now."},
    {t:"narr", text:"At nine the lanterns come down. Rodrigo has spent the evening at the end of Chiyo's counter, drawing her customers for nothing."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"rodrigo", ja:"ちよさん、ポスターは[明日]{あした}はがしますか。", en:"Chiyo-san, does the poster come down tomorrow?", gl:"はがす: to peel off, to take down."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"chiyo", ja:"はがしませんよ。[来年]{らいねん}、日にちだけ書き[直]{なお}させますから。", en:"It does not. Next year I shall just have you redo the date.", gl:"日にち (ひにち): the date. 書き直す (かきなおす): to rewrite. 書き直させる: to have someone rewrite."},
    {t:"line", mood:"yay", who:"rodrigo", ja:"[来年]{らいねん}…！はい！書かせてください！", en:"Next year...! Yes! Please let me!", gl:"書かせてください: please let me write it. Causative + ください asks for permission."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Whether there is a next year is not Chiyo's to promise. But a date is a small thing to redo, and she has ordered it. Out on the step, exactly where the poster put her, a black-and-white cat is washing a paw. By Monday the pencil tally on the noticeboard at Kamome House has gone up by one."},
    {t:"cat", pose:"stretch", alt:"The cat stretching happily on the tea-shop step"},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u7-x1", type:"mcq", q:"Toby says [源]{げん}さんにイカを[焼]{や}かされて、[岩田]{いわた}さんにビールを[飲]{の}まされた. Who grilled the squid?", options:[
      {t:"Toby, because Gen-san made him", ok:true, why:"Right. [焼]{や}かされる is the causative-passive of [焼]{や}く: *to be made to grill*. The person who gives the order takes に ([源]{げん}さんに), and the person who does the work is the subject, here Toby."},
      {t:"Gen-san, as a treat for Toby", why:"A favour would be [源]{げん}さんがイカを[焼]{や}いてくれた. With [焼]{や}かされた, Toby did the grilling and did not choose to."},
      {t:"Gen-san, because Toby made him", why:"That would be the plain causative: [源]{げん}さんにイカを[焼]{や}かせた. The passive ending on top, [焼]{や}かされた, turns it round: Toby was the one made to."},
      {t:"Mr Iwata", why:"Mr Iwata comes in the second half of the sentence, and his job was the beer: ビールを[飲]{の}まされた, *I was made to drink*."}]}},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u7-x2", type:"mcq", q:"Rodrigo says まつりは今年で[終]{お}わるらしいですね. How does he know?", options:[
      {t:"He has heard people saying so", ok:true, why:"Right. ～らしい passes on what you have heard or read, without claiming it as your own knowledge. He even gives his source: パン[屋]{や}さんで[聞]{き}きました."},
      {t:"He can see it with his own eyes", why:"For something you can see coming, use the ます-stem + そう: [終]{お}わりそう, *it looks about to end*. らしい is for what you have heard."},
      {t:"Chiyo has just told him", why:"He is the one telling Chiyo, and she is not impressed: [去年]{きょねん}もそう言われましたよ."},
      {t:"He has decided it himself", why:"らしい never reports your own decision. It keeps the speaker at a distance from the news: *apparently*, *they say*."}]}},
    {t:"lang", items:["The passive leaves people out: この[通]{とお}りでは「まっちゃ」と[呼]{よ}ばれています (*she is called Matcha*) and [去年]{きょねん}もそう言われました (*that was said last year too*). Nobody has to say who does the calling or the saying. When the person matters, に marks them: ちよさんに[頼]{たの}まれて.", "Make, and be made to: Chiyo will make Rodrigo redo the date (書き[直]{なお}させます), and Mariya will make Toby say no (言わせる). Turn it round and you get the causative-passive, for the person on the receiving end: 行かされた, [焼]{や}かされて, [飲]{の}まされた, [話]{はな}させられた.", "How do you know? まちがえそう (*I can tell I'm going to get it wrong*), [終]{お}わるらしい (*people say it will end*) and [通]{つう}じたみたい (*it seems to have got through*, judging by what she saw). Three endings for three kinds of evidence."]},
    {t:"reflect", q:"Mariya speaks English only once Toby has left the table. Have you ever found you could do something because the person you were relying on wasn't there?"}
  ]},
  {unit:"e3u8", n:8, title:"The hazard map", month:"September", level:"N4", parts:[
    {t:"narr", text:"*Previously at Kamome House:* Rodrigo's poster filled Swallow Street for a festival that may or may not have been its last. Mariya spoke English to strangers, and Toby promised the same seven o'clock to two old fishermen who haven't spoken in thirty years."},
    {t:"narr", text:"The first Sunday of September. The typhoons have so far left Shioura alone, and the Satōs have crossed the garden for dinner as usual. When the bowls are cleared, Cheska puts a sheet of paper on the low table, where a dessert would go, and unfolds it all the way. She has carried it folded since June."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"cheska", ja:"みんな、ちょっといい？これ、[市役所]{しやくしょ}でもらった[地図]{ちず}なんだけど。", en:"Everyone, have you got a minute? This is a map I got at the city office.", gl:"市役所 (しやくしょ): the city office."},
    {t:"plates", title:"The map", hint:"Read each line of the map, then tap it to check.", items:[
      {ja:"汐浦市 内水ハザードマップ", ro:"しおうらし ないすい ハザードマップ", who:"The Shioura *naisui* hazard map. 内 is *inside* and 水 is *water*. Japanese cities publish hazard maps like this one, and they are free at the city office."},
      {ja:"赤：〇・五メートル以上", ro:"あか：れいてんご メートル いじょう", who:"Red: water half a metre deep or more. 以上 means *that much or more*, and it includes the number. Half a metre is about knee height, which is enough to make walking dangerous."},
      {ja:"避難所：東小学校", ro:"ひなんじょ：ひがし しょうがっこう", who:"Evacuation shelter: East Primary School. 避難 (ひなん) is getting away from danger, and 所 is a place. Neither kanji of 避難 is on the N4 list, but this is a word to know by sight. The school stands on the rise behind the old town, fifteen minutes away on foot."},
      {ja:"大雨のときは、早めにひなんしましょう", ro:"おおあめの ときは、はやめに ひなんしましょう", who:"*In heavy rain, evacuate early.* 早め is *on the early side*: before you are sure you need to."}]},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"cheska", ja:"「うちみず…ハザードマップ」。", en:"\"Uchi-mizu... hazard map.\""},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"toby", ja:"「ないすい」だよ。「[内]{うち}」に「水」と書いて、「ないすい」。", en:"It's \"naisui\". You write \"inside\" and \"water\", and read it \"naisui\"."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"cheska", ja:"ありがとう。川の水じゃなくて、[町]{まち}の[中]{なか}に[降]{ふ}った雨の水のこと。", en:"Thanks. It doesn't mean river water. It means the rain that falls inside the town.", gl:"降る (ふる): to fall, of rain or snow."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"cheska", ja:"大雨で川の水が[高]{たか}くなると、川の[門]{もん}が[閉]{し}まる。すると、[町]{まち}の水は[外]{そと}に出られない。", en:"When heavy rain makes the river rise, the gates on the river close. Then the water in the town can't get out.", gl:"門 (もん): a gate. She means the sluice gates (水門, すいもん) in the river bank. 閉まる (しまる): to close. すると: and then."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"rodrigo", ja:"この[家]{いえ}はどこ？", en:"Where's this house?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"cheska", ja:"ここ。[赤]{あか}い[所]{ところ}。", en:"Here. In the red."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Nobody speaks. Rodrigo holds a hand at half a metre against his own leg and looks at it. On the map the red runs from the river to the foot of the hill, over the house, the bus stop and the whole of Swallow Street."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"rodrigo", ja:"じゃあ、[白]{しろ}い[所]{ところ}は[安全]{あんぜん}？", en:"So the white parts are safe?", gl:"安全 (あんぜん): safe."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"cheska", ja:"[白]{しろ}は「[安全]{あんぜん}」という[意味]{いみ}じゃないよ。「ここまでは来ないと[思]{おも}う」という[意味]{いみ}。", en:"White doesn't mean \"safe\". It means \"we don't think it will come this far\".", gl:"意味 (いみ): meaning. ～という意味: it means ～."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Toby has been turning his phone over in his hand. Since June he has spent his Saturdays at the harbour with a recorder, collecting the old Shioura dialect before the last of its speakers are gone. Give an old fisherman a microphone and he talks about weather."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"toby", ja:"チェスカ、[源]{げん}さんの[話]{はなし}も[聞]{き}いてくれる？子どものとき、この[町]{まち}で大きい水が出たんだって。", en:"Cheska, would you listen to Gen-san's story too? He says there was a big flood in this town when he was a child.", gl:"水が出る: \"water came out\", an everyday way to say a place flooded."},
    {t:"narr", text:"He presses play. A very old voice fills the room, in a Japanese that no textbook covers. The Satōs follow every word. Toby puts it into the standard kind for everyone else."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"toby", ja:"「水は川から来なかった。[道]{みち}の[下]{した}から来た」。", en:"\"The water didn't come from the river. It came up from under the road.\""},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"toby", ja:"「[夕方]{ゆうがた}に[始]{はじ}まって、[朝]{あさ}まで[止]{と}まらなかった。でも、つばめ[通]{どお}りまでは来なかった」。", en:"\"It started in the evening and didn't stop till morning. But it never came as far as Swallow Street.\""},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"cheska", ja:"…それは[何年前]{なんねんまえ}の[話]{はなし}？", en:"...How long ago was this?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"toby", ja:"[七十年]{ななじゅうねん}ぐらい[前]{まえ}。[源]{げん}さんが[九]{きゅう}さいのとき。", en:"About seventy years. Gen-san was nine."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"cheska", ja:"[七十年前]{ななじゅうねんまえ}の[思]{おも}い[出]{で}は、データじゃないよ。今はポンプもあるし、[道]{みち}も[新]{あたら}しいし。[地図]{ちず}では、つばめ[通]{どお}りも[赤]{あか}。", en:"A memory from seventy years ago isn't data. There are pumps now, and the roads are new. On the map, Swallow Street is red too.", gl:"思い出 (おもいで): a memory. データ: data. ポンプ: a pump."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Toby agrees with people. It is what he does, and the table waits for him to do it."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"toby", ja:"…でも、この[地図]{ちず}を[作]{つく}った[人]{ひと}は、その水を見てないよ。[源]{げん}さんは、その[中]{なか}を[歩]{ある}いたんだ。", en:"...But whoever made this map never saw that water. Gen-san walked through it."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Cheska has an answer to that. It is a long one, it has nothing to do with Shioura, and she doesn't use it."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"cheska", ja:"…[地図]{ちず}は[計算]{けいさん}だよ。[一番]{いちばん}[悪]{わる}い雨のときの。", en:"...A map is a calculation. Of the worst rain there could be.", gl:"計算 (けいさん): a calculation."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"toby", ja:"[話]{はなし}は[一回]{いっかい}だけだね。[本当]{ほんとう}に[降]{ふ}った雨の。", en:"And a story is only the once. Of a rain that really fell.", gl:"本当に (ほんとうに): really."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Each of them has just said what is wrong with their own evidence. In this house that counts as a fight. Mr Satō has been reading the map upside down from the far side of the table."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"shoichi", ja:"[源]{げん}の[話]{はなし}は[本当]{ほんとう}だ。おれも見た。つばめ[通]{どお}りは[昔]{むかし}の[堤防]{ていぼう}の[上]{うえ}だから、[少]{すこ}し[高]{たか}い。", en:"Gen's story is true. I saw it too. Swallow Street runs along the top of the old sea wall, so it's a little higher.", gl:"昔 (むかし): long ago. 堤防 (ていぼう): an embankment or sea wall."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Three hundred years ago the street was the shore. The rise is four steps at most, and the map's squares are too big to notice it. Cheska looks at the old man, and then at the map. She borrows the pencil Mrs Satō keeps for the cat tally, draws a line along Swallow Street, and writes beside it: 源さんの話. Print for the calculation, pencil for what somebody saw."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"cheska", ja:"じゃあ、[学校]{がっこう}へは、川の[道]{みち}じゃなくて、つばめ[通]{どお}りを[通]{とお}って行こう。", en:"Then let's go to the school by Swallow Street, not by the river road."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"toby", ja:"うん。それから、[地図]{ちず}の言う[通]{とお}り、[早]{はや}めに出よう。[源]{げん}さんの[家族]{かぞく}は、[朝]{あさ}まで[二階]{にかい}から[下]{お}りられなかったんだって。", en:"Yes. And let's leave early, as the map says. Gen-san's family couldn't come down from upstairs till morning.", gl:"～の言う通り (とおり): just as ～ says. 二階 (にかい): upstairs, the first floor. 下りる (おりる): to come down."},
    {t:"narr", text:"The route from the story, and the timing from the map. Mr Satō, meanwhile, has put a finger on the first kanji of the title, the one that has needed furigana all year."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"shoichi", ja:"さんずいに、[夕方]{ゆうがた}の[夕]{ゆう}。「[汐]{しお}」は[夕方]{ゆうがた}のしおだ。[朝]{あさ}のしおは、[別]{べつ}の[字]{じ}を書く。", en:"The water radical, and the \"evening\" of yūgata. 汐 is the evening tide. The morning tide is written with a different character.", gl:"さんずい: the name of 氵, the three-stroke *water* part on the left of a kanji. しお: the tide. 別の字 (べつのじ): a different character."},
    {t:"note", text:"汐 is not on any JLPT list, which is why Shioura has worn furigana since April. But you can take it apart now: 氵 is water and 夕 is evening. Japanese has two kanji for the tide, 潮 for the morning and 汐 for the evening, and this town was named after the second. A kanji you can't read is very often two that you can."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Cheska doesn't fold the map again. It goes up on the noticeboard beside the cat tally, pencil line and all. By morning there is one more line at the bottom, in a retired teacher's hand: 九人で行きましょう. Nine is seven residents and two Satōs. It is not a suggestion. Mr Satō reads it on his way past the barometer, taps the glass, and keeps his opinion to himself."},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u8-x1", type:"mcq", q:"On the map, Kamome House is in a 赤 area: 〇・五メートル以上. What does that tell the residents?", options:[
      {t:"In the worst rain, the water there could be half a metre deep or more", ok:true, why:"Right. 以上 is *that much or more*, and it includes the number itself. Cheska adds what the map is: [一番]{いちばん}[悪]{わる}い雨のときの[計算]{けいさん}, a calculation for the worst rain."},
      {t:"The water there will be less than half a metre deep", why:"*Half a metre or less* would be 〇・五メートル以下. 以上 points the other way: from the number upwards."},
      {t:"The house is half a metre higher than the river", why:"The number is the depth of the water, not the height of the land. The red is where water could stand half a metre deep or more."},
      {t:"The house is in a safe area", why:"On this map colour means risk. And even white is not a promise: [白]{しろ}は「[安全]{あんぜん}」という[意味]{いみ}じゃないよ."}]}},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u8-x2", type:"type", q:"Cheska first reads 内水 as うちみず. Type the reading Toby gives her, in hiragana.", book:"Write the reading of 内水 (flooding from rain trapped inside the river bank) in hiragana.", answer:"ないすい",
      hint:"In a two-kanji word, both kanji usually take their on-readings. 水 is スイ, as in 水よう日.",
      wrongs:[{v:"うちみず", why:"Those are the kun-readings, the ones each kanji has when it stands alone: [内]{うち}, [水]{みず}. Inside a two-kanji word they usually switch to the on-readings: ナイ and スイ."},{v:"ないみず", why:"Half right: 内 is ナイ here. But 水 takes its on-reading too, スイ, as in 水よう日."}],
      why:"ないすい: 内 (ナイ, inside) + 水 (スイ, water). Alone they are [内]{うち} and [水]{みず}; together they take their on-readings."}},
    {t:"lang", items:["Kun and on: Cheska reads 内水 as うちみず, one kanji at a time. As a word it is ないすい. The same thing happens with 大雨 (おおあめ, both kun) and [地図]{ちず} (both on), so a new compound is always worth checking.", "Things that happen by themselves: 川の[門]{もん}が[閉]{し}まる, [夕方]{ゆうがた}に[始]{はじ}まって, [朝]{あさ}まで[止]{と}まらなかった. These are the intransitive halves of [閉]{し}める・[閉]{し}まる, [始]{はじ}める・[始]{はじ}まる and [止]{と}める・[止]{と}まる. Nobody in the sentence closes, starts or stops anything, so they take が.", "One kanji, several jobs: 通 is the street in つばめ[通]{どお}り, the verb in [通]{とお}って行こう, and *just as* in [地図]{ちず}の言う[通]{とお}り. In a street name とおり becomes どおり."]},
    {t:"reflect", q:"Cheska trusts the map and Toby trusts the fisherman, and in the end they use both. When you have to decide something, which do you reach for first: the numbers, or someone who was there?"}
  ]},
  {unit:"e3u9", n:9, title:"The night of the rain", month:"September", level:"N3", parts:[
    {t:"narr", text:"*Previously at Kamome House:* Cheska unfolded the city's hazard map at Sunday dinner. The house kept the map's advice to leave early and an old fisherman's route along Swallow Street, and Mrs Satō wrote 九人で行きましょう at the bottom in pencil."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Sixteen days later it rains. Not hard, at first; it simply doesn't move. Yến has had the university's rain gauge open in a tab since lunch, and has stopped reading the numbers out. The cat has not come for her saucer. At ten to seven every phone in the house goes off at once."},
    {t:"plates", title:"The alert", hint:"Read each line of the alert, then tap it to check.", items:[
      {ja:"【警戒レベル3】高齢者等避難", ro:"けいかいレベル さん こうれいしゃとう ひなん", who:"*Alert Level 3: older people and others, evacuate.* 警戒 is being on guard, 高齢者 is older people, and 等 means *and others*: anyone who needs extra time. The city issues it. It tells them to go now, and everyone else to get ready."},
      {ja:"大雨のため、内水氾濫のおそれがあります", ro:"おおあめの ため、ないすいはんらんの おそれが あります", who:"*Because of heavy rain, there is a risk of flooding inside the river bank.* 氾濫 (はんらん) is water overflowing, and おそれ is a risk. This ～のため gives a cause: the formal *because of* that notices use."},
      {ja:"対象：旧市街の全域", ro:"たいしょう：きゅうしがいの ぜんいき", who:"*Applies to: the whole of the old town.* That is the red on Cheska's map."},
      {ja:"避難所：東小学校 体育館", ro:"ひなんじょ：ひがししょうがっこう たいいくかん", who:"*Shelter: the gym at East Primary School.*"}]},
    {t:"narr", text:"Mrs Satō is already in the hall in a raincoat. She runs the neighbourhood association's group chat."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"fumiko", ja:"[水門]{すいもん}が[閉]{し}まったそうです。[町内会]{ちょうないかい}のチャットに書いてありました。", en:"They say the sluice gates have closed. It was in the neighbourhood association's chat.", gl:"水門 (すいもん): a sluice gate. 町内会 (ちょうないかい): the neighbourhood association."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"fumiko", ja:"それから、「[高齢者]{こうれいしゃ}」というのは、主人と私のことですね。", en:"And \"older people\", I take it, means my husband and me.", gl:"高齢者 (こうれいしゃ): older people, the elderly. 主人 (しゅじん): my husband."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Everyone looks at Cheska."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"cheska", ja:"レベル3は、さとうさんたちにとって「今すぐ」という意味です。でも私は、[安全]{あんぜん}のために、[全員]{ぜんいん}で今出るべきだと思います。", en:"For you and Mr Satō, Level 3 means \"right now\". But to be safe, I think all of us should leave now.", gl:"全員 (ぜんいん): everyone, all of us. 今すぐ: right now."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"cheska", ja:"[内水]{ないすい}は、始まると早いから。出るのは、早ければ早いほどいい。", en:"Once this kind of flooding starts, it's quick. The earlier we go, the better."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"cheska", ja:"…でも、これは私の意見。みんなに[決]{き}めてほしい。", en:"...But that's my opinion. I want all of you to decide.", gl:"決める (きめる): to decide."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Her voice is level, the voice of someone who has done this before, in another language. Then she stops, which costs her more than going on would."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"fumiko", ja:"主人と私は、行くことにしました。", en:"My husband and I have decided to go."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Mr Satō is in the doorway behind her with his cap on, having tapped the barometer on the way in. The rest decide the way this house decides things, by doing. Toby, who grew up on an island and cannot swim, has had his shoes on since the alarm. Only Aoi is standing still, with her phone at her ear."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"cheska", ja:"あおい、[手伝]{てつだ}って。下の物を[二階]{にかい}に[上]{あ}げたいの。", en:"Aoi, give us a hand. I want to get the downstairs things up to the first floor."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"aoi", ja:"ごめん、今、おばあちゃんに電話しているところ。[三回]{さんかい}かけたのに、出ないの。", en:"Sorry, I'm in the middle of calling my grandmother. I've tried three times and she isn't picking up.", gl:"～ているところ: right in the middle of doing. 電話に出る: to answer the phone."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Cheska had a sentence ready, about who carries things in this house and who doesn't. She puts it away."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"aoi", ja:"…あ、出た。おばあちゃん？うん。うん。動かないで。今から行くから。", en:"...Oh, she's picked up. Grandma? Yes. Yes. Don't move. I'm coming now."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"aoi", ja:"チェスカ、私は学校じゃなくて、おばあちゃんの[所]{ところ}に行くことにする。店の[二階]{にかい}だし、つばめ通りは少し高いはずだから。", en:"Cheska, I've decided to go to my grandmother's, not the school. She's above the shop, and Swallow Street ought to be a little higher."},
    {t:"narr", text:"That is not the plan. The plan is nine to the school, in pencil."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"cheska", ja:"…[本当]{ほんとう}は、[全員]{ぜんいん}で学校に行ってほしい。", en:"...Honestly, I want all of us to go to the school."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"aoi", ja:"分かってる。でも、おばあちゃんは[一人]{ひとり}で[階段]{かいだん}を[下]{お}りられないの。雨の中を学校まで歩かせたくない。", en:"I know. But she can't get down the stairs by herself. And I don't want to make her walk to the school in this rain.", gl:"階段 (かいだん): stairs."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"cheska", ja:"…分かった。[二階]{にかい}から[下]{お}りないで。着いたら、すぐ[連絡]{れんらく}して。", en:"...All right. Don't come down from upstairs. And message me the minute you get there.", gl:"連絡 (れんらく)する: to get in touch."},
    {t:"narr", text:"It is Aoi's grandmother, and Aoi's call. What can be lifted goes upstairs: the rice cooker, eleven bottles of ink. Mrs Satō comes back across the garden with her handbag and a biscuit tin."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"cheska", ja:"はぐれないように、[二人]{ふたり}ずつ歩いて。川の道じゃなくて、つばめ通りを通って行くよ。", en:"Walk in pairs, so nobody gets separated. We're going by Swallow Street, not the river road.", gl:"はぐれる: to get separated from the people you are with. ～ずつ: ～ at a time."},
    {t:"narr", text:"They leave at twenty past seven. At the corner the water is coming *up*: it stands over a drain cover in a dome, like a spring. Toby looks at it, then at Cheska. Neither of them says *Gen-san*. Under the roof of Swallow Street the ground is still dry. Aoi turns off at the tea shop, and eight people climb the hill."},
    {t:"narr", text:"The shelter is a school gym, with a man from the city office holding a list. Mrs Satō taught in this building and tells him where the blankets are. The lights stay on all night, here and across the old town below, which is strange to look at: a flood with the street lamps working. At half past nine the phones go again."},
    {t:"plates", title:"The second alert", hint:"Read each line, then tap it to check.", items:[
      {ja:"【警戒レベル4】避難指示", ro:"けいかいレベル よん ひなんしじ", who:"*Alert Level 4: evacuation instruction.* Everyone in the area should get to somewhere safe. There is a Level 5, but it is not a signal to leave: it means the disaster is already happening. The rule is to be out by Level 4."},
      {ja:"旧市街で道路が冠水しています", ro:"きゅうしがいで どうろが かんすい しています", who:"*Roads in the old town are under water.* 道路 (どうろ) is a road, and 冠水 (かんすい) is being covered with water."}]},
    {t:"narr", text:"Kamome House has been on the gym mats for two hours by then. Nobody mentions having been early. Aoi's message came long ago: 着いた。 Cheska has found a table that needs someone, the one with the towels. She is still at it at half past ten, when six young women in fish-plant jackets come in out of the dark, wet to the knee. The one in front has her phone in a freezer bag."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"cheska", ja:"こんばんは。タオルをどうぞ。[何人]{なんにん}ですか。", en:"Good evening. Have a towel. How many of you are there?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"siti", ja:"ありがとうございます。六人です。魚の工場の[寮]{りょう}から来ました。シティです。", en:"Thank you. Six. We've come from the dormitory at the fish plant. I'm Siti.", gl:"寮 (りょう): a dormitory. 工場 (こうじょう): a factory, a plant."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"cheska", ja:"チェスカです。[寮]{りょう}の人は、これで[全員]{ぜんいん}ですか。", en:"I'm Cheska. Is this everyone from the dormitory?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"siti", ja:"はい。[数]{かぞ}えました。[全員]{ぜんいん}います。", en:"Yes. I counted. Everyone is here.", gl:"数える (かぞえる): to count."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Siti Rahayu is from Indonesia and Cheska is from the Philippines. The language they share tonight is Japanese."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"cheska", ja:"スマホのアラームは[鳴]{な}りましたか。", en:"Did the alarm on your phones go off?", gl:"鳴る (なる): to sound, to ring."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"siti", ja:"[鳴]{な}りました。大きい音で、[二回]{にかい}。でも、漢字ばかりで、だれも読めませんでした。", en:"It did. Loudly, twice. But it was all kanji, and none of us could read it.", gl:"～ばかり: nothing but ～."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"siti", ja:"「ひなん」という[言葉]{ことば}は知っています。聞けば分かります。でも、字は読めないんです。", en:"I know the word hinan. If I hear it, I understand. But I can't read the characters.", gl:"言葉 (ことば): a word; language."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"cheska", ja:"会社から[連絡]{れんらく}はありませんでしたか。", en:"Didn't the company get in touch?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"siti", ja:"[寮]{りょう}には、会社の人が知らせることになっています。でも、今日は工場が休みで、だれも来ませんでした。", en:"Someone from the company is supposed to tell the dormitory. But the plant was closed today, and nobody came.", gl:"知らせる (しらせる): to let someone know. ～ことになっている: it is the arrangement that ～."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"cheska", ja:"じゃあ、どうして分かったんですか。", en:"Then how did you find out?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"siti", ja:"友だちのおかげです。別の[寮]{りょう}の友だちが、ボイスメッセージを送ってくれました。「水が来るよ、学校に行って」って。インドネシア語で。", en:"Thanks to a friend. A friend in another dormitory sent us a voice message: \"The water's coming, go to the school.\" In Indonesian.", gl:"ボイスメッセージ: a voice message."},
    {t:"narr", text:"By then the water was at the dormitory step. They walked up the hill in a line, each holding the sleeve in front, on a road they couldn't see."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"siti", ja:"もっと早く、分かる[言葉]{ことば}で知らせてほしかったです。", en:"I wish they had told us sooner, in words we could understand."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"cheska", ja:"…そうですね。読めなかったのは、シティさんたちのせいじゃありません。知らせ[方]{かた}のせいです。", en:"...Yes. It isn't your fault that you couldn't read it. It's the fault of the way it was sent.", gl:"知らせ方 (しらせかた): the way of telling people."},
    {t:"narr", text:"This happens to be what Cheska came to Japan to study. Tonight she doesn't write it down. She finds six blankets."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"siti", ja:"[寮]{りょう}は[大丈夫]{だいじょうぶ}でしょうか。", en:"Do you think the dormitory will be all right?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"cheska", ja:"分かりません。朝まで、だれにも分からないと思います。うちも同じです。", en:"I don't know. I don't think anyone will know until morning. It's the same for our house."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Two in the morning. Mr Satō sleeps sitting up, as a man does after forty years of engine rooms. Mrs Satō is awake beside him with the tin on her knees. Cheska's phone lights up."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"aoi", ja:"起きてる？水は店の前の[段]{だん}で止まったよ。中には入ってない。", en:"You awake? The water's stopped at the step in front of the shop. It hasn't come in.", gl:"段 (だん): a step."},
    {t:"line", mood:"yay", who:"aoi", ja:"写真を送るね。[段]{だん}の上に、だれがいると思う？", en:"I'm sending a photo. Guess who's on the step?"},
    {t:"narr", text:"A street's width of brown water under the arcade roof. Above it, on the one dry step, sits a black-and-white cat, looking personally inconvenienced."},
    {t:"cat", pose:"worried", alt:"The cat on the dry step, giving the water a side-eye"},
    {t:"line", mood:"yay", who:"cheska", ja:"…ミンミン！", en:"...Mingming!"},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"aoi", ja:"おばあちゃんは「うちのまっちゃ」って言ってるけどね。", en:"Grandma is calling her \"our Matcha\", mind you."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"cheska", ja:"そこから、家の[方]{ほう}は見える？", en:"Can you see towards the house from there?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"aoi", ja:"見えない。そっちの道は、[全部]{ぜんぶ}水の下。電気はついてるのに。", en:"No. The road that way is all under water. Even though the lights are on.", gl:"全部 (ぜんぶ): all of it."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"cheska", ja:"…ポンプは動いているはず。雨も、もうすぐ[止]{や}むはず。", en:"...The pumps should be running. And the rain should stop soon.", gl:"止む (やむ): to stop, of rain or snow. Same kanji as 止まる, different verb."},
    {t:"note", text:"はず is for what you have good reason to expect and no way of checking. つばめ通りは少し高いはず. ポンプは動いているはず. On a night like this, nearly every sentence about the next few hours needs one, and the honest speakers put it in."},
    {t:"narr", text:"She lays the phone face up on the mat, where she can see it, and doesn't lie down. At the far end of the gym Siti is recording a message for somebody, quietly. It is still raining, though less. What is standing in the hall of Kamome House tonight, nobody here knows. They will know in the morning."},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u9-x1", type:"mcq", q:"The first alert says 【[警戒]{けいかい}レベル3】[高齢者]{こうれいしゃ}[等]{とう}[避難]{ひなん}. What is it asking people in the old town to do?", options:[
      {t:"Older people, and anyone else who needs extra time, should evacuate now; everyone else should get ready", ok:true, why:"Right. [高齢者]{こうれいしゃ} is older people and [等]{とう} adds *and others*. At Kamome House that means the Satōs, as Mrs Satō points out herself. The others could have waited, and decide not to."},
      {t:"Everyone should wait indoors for Level 5", why:"Level 5 is not a signal to leave. It means the disaster is already happening, so the aim is to be somewhere safe before then."},
      {t:"Only people over seventy-five need to do anything", why:"The alert gives no age, and [等]{とう} widens it to anyone who needs time: small children, people who are ill, people who walk slowly. Everyone else is being told to get ready."},
      {t:"Everyone must leave the old town at once", why:"That is Level 4, [避難指示]{ひなんしじ}, which arrives at half past nine. Level 3 starts with the people who need the most time."}]}},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u9-x2", type:"mcq", q:"Siti says [寮]{りょう}には、会社の人が知らせることになっています. What does ことになっています tell you?", options:[
      {t:"It is the arrangement: someone from the company is supposed to tell the dormitory", ok:true, why:"Right. ～ことになっている describes a rule or an arrangement that somebody else has set. Tonight the arrangement existed and nobody was there to carry it out."},
      {t:"Siti has decided to tell the dormitory herself", why:"Your own decision is ～ことにする, as in Aoi's おばあちゃんの[所]{ところ}に行くことにする. ことになっている is a decision made for you."},
      {t:"Someone from the company told the dormitory tonight", why:"She goes on: でも、今日は工場が休みで、だれも来ませんでした. The rule says someone should; tonight nobody did."},
      {t:"The company will tell the dormitory from now on", why:"That would be a new decision: 知らせることになりました. ～ことになっています describes how things already stand."}]}},
    {t:"lang", items:["Who decided? 行くことにしました (Mrs Satō) and おばあちゃんの[所]{ところ}に行くことにする (Aoi) are the speaker's own decisions. 会社の人が知らせることになっています is an arrangement somebody else made, and Siti can only report it.", "An opinion and a wish: 今出るべきだと思います says what Cheska believes is right. みんなに[決]{き}めてほしい and 学校に行ってほしい say what she wants other people to do. ～てほしい is a wish, not an order, which is why Aoi can answer 分かってる and still go to her grandmother's.", "Credit and blame: 友だちのおかげです gives a friend the credit for a good result. シティさんたちのせいじゃありません。知らせ[方]{かた}のせいです moves the blame off the people and onto the way the warning was sent."]},
    {t:"reflect", q:"Cheska says what she thinks the house should do, and then says みんなに[決]{き}めてほしい. When you are the person in the room who knows the most, how do you decide what to leave to everyone else?"}
  ]},
  {unit:"e3u10", n:10, title:"After the water", month:"Late October–November", level:"N3", parts:[
    {t:"narr", text:"*Previously at Kamome House:* On the night of the rain the house left early for the school gym. Siti's dormitory got an alarm that nobody there could read. The water stopped at the tea shop's step, and at two in the morning nobody knew about the house."},
    {t:"narr", text:"In the morning they knew. The water had come twelve centimetres over the floor downstairs and gone again by the drains, leaving a brown line round the hall. Above it the barometer was dry and, Mr Satō reported, correct. The cat was on the fourth stair, and declined to come lower."},
    {t:"cat", pose:"worried", alt:"The black-and-white cat on the fourth stair, giving the wet hall a sideways look."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Bedding from three rooms and the living-room tatami went out to the kerb. For three weeks Cheska ran the clean-up with photographs, lists and a rota. Then everything was dry, and there was nothing left to organise."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Mid-October. After a flood, most help starts with the city's certificate of damage, and Mrs Satō has sent Aoi and Cheska to apply for it. The man at the disaster-prevention counter is the one who held the list in the gym. He looks as if he hasn't been home since."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"matsumoto", ja:"四十七[番]{ばん}の[方]{かた}、お待たせいたしました。[防災課]{ぼうさいか}の[松本]{まつもと}と[申]{もう}します。", en:"Number forty-seven, thank you for waiting. My name is Matsumoto, from the disaster-prevention section.", gl:"防災課 (ぼうさいか): the disaster-prevention section. ～と申します: the humble *my name is*."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"aoi", ja:"[罹災証明書]{りさいしょうめいしょ}の[申請]{しんせい}に[参]{まい}りました。[大家]{おおや}の[佐藤]{さとう}さんの[代理]{だいり}です。", en:"We've come to apply for a certificate of disaster damage. We're here on behalf of our landlady, Mrs Satō.", gl:"罹災証明書 (りさいしょうめいしょ): the city's certificate that a home was damaged in a disaster. 申請 (しんせい): an application. 参る (まいる): the humble *come*. 大家 (おおや): a landlord or landlady. 代理 (だいり): someone acting for another person."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"matsumoto", ja:"かしこまりました。[被害]{ひがい}の分かるお写真はお持ちですか。", en:"Certainly. Do you have photographs that show the damage?", gl:"被害 (ひがい): damage. お持ちですか: the respectful *do you have?*"},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"cheska", ja:"はい。[片付]{かたづ}ける前に[撮]{と}ったものがございます。水は[床]{ゆか}の上、十二センチまで来ておりました。", en:"Yes. We have some that were taken before we cleared up. The water had come to twelve centimetres above the floor.", gl:"片付ける (かたづける): to clear up. 撮る (とる): to take a photo. 床 (ゆか): the floor. ございます, おります: the very polite あります and the humble います."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Photograph first, clean second. Cheska has taught that sentence to rooms full of people, in two other languages."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"matsumoto", ja:"[助]{たす}かります。[調査]{ちょうさ}に[伺]{うかが}うのは、三週間ほど先になりますが、よろしいでしょうか。", en:"That is a great help. It will be about three weeks before we can come and inspect. Would that be all right?", gl:"調査 (ちょうさ): an inspection, a survey. 伺う (うかがう): the humble *visit* or *ask*. ～ほど: about ～."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"cheska", ja:"…三週間ですか。では、一つ[伺]{うかが}います。あの夜のアラートは、日本語だけでお送りになりましたね。", en:"...Three weeks. Then may I ask one thing. The alerts that night were sent in Japanese only, weren't they.", gl:"お送りになる: the respectful *send*."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"matsumoto", ja:"はい。[決]{き}まりの[通]{とお}りに、お送りいたしました。", en:"Yes. We sent them as the rules lay down.", gl:"決まり (きまり): the rules. ～の通りに (とおりに): just as ～. お送りいたす: the humble *send*."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"cheska", ja:"お送りになっても、読めなければ、[届]{とど}いたわけではありません。魚の工場の[寮]{りょう}では、「[避難]{ひなん}」という字さえ、だれも読めなかったんです。", en:"Even if you sent them, if they can't be read, it doesn't follow that they arrived. At the fish plant dormitory, nobody could read even the characters for \"evacuate\".", gl:"届く (とどく): to arrive, to reach someone. 寮 (りょう): a dormitory. 避難 (ひなん): evacuation."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Every verb is correct. A person can be furious in keigo, it turns out; the grammar holds. Aoi puts a hand flat on the counter."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"aoi", ja:"[申]{もう}し[訳]{わけ}ありません。[松本]{まつもと}さんを[責]{せ}めているわけではないんです。", en:"I do apologise. It isn't that we're blaming you, Mr Matsumoto.", gl:"責める (せめる): to blame."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"matsumoto", ja:"…いいえ、おっしゃる[通]{とお}りです。あの[寮]{りょう}の[方]{かた}たちが[体育館]{たいいくかん}にいらっしゃったとき、私は[受付]{うけつけ}におりました。", en:"...No. It is just as you say. When the people from that dormitory came into the gym, I was at the reception table.", gl:"おっしゃる: the respectful *say*. いらっしゃる: the respectful *come*, *go* or *be*. 受付 (うけつけ): reception."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"matsumoto", ja:"[実]{じつ}は、その[件]{けん}で、大学の先生[方]{がた}にご[相談]{そうだん}したいと考えております。", en:"As it happens, we are hoping to consult the university about exactly that.", gl:"実は (じつは): as a matter of fact. その件 (けん): that matter. ご相談する: the humble *consult*."},
    {t:"narr", text:"He means their supervisor, Prof. Ōnishi, and Yến's and Kaito's, Dr Amoako. Outside, Aoi sits on the bench by the bus stop until Cheska sits too."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"aoi", ja:"さっきのチェスカ、ちょっとこわかったよ。[敬語]{けいご}なのに。", en:"You were a bit frightening in there. And in keigo, too.", gl:"敬語 (けいご): keigo, polite and honorific language."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"cheska", ja:"ごめん。[最近]{さいきん}、[寝不足]{ねぶそく}[気味]{ぎみ}なだけ。[大丈夫]{だいじょうぶ}。", en:"Sorry. I'm a little short of sleep lately, that's all. I'm fine.", gl:"寝不足 (ねぶそく): not enough sleep. ～気味 (ぎみ): a touch of ～."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"aoi", ja:"「[大丈夫]{だいじょうぶ}？」とは聞いてないけど。", en:"I didn't ask whether you were fine."},
    {t:"narr", text:"A bus comes and goes."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"aoi", ja:"…じゃあ、私が先に言うね。「おばあちゃんのために[汐浦]{しおうら}に来た」って、みんなに言ってるでしょ。あれは、[半分]{はんぶん}だけ。", en:"...All right, I'll go first. You know how I tell everyone I came to Shioura for my grandmother? That's only half of it.", gl:"半分 (はんぶん): half."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"aoi", ja:"東京の[大学院]{だいがくいん}に[落]{お}ちたの。入れたのは、ここだけだった。", en:"I failed the entrance exam for graduate school in Tokyo. This was the only place I got into.", gl:"大学院 (だいがくいん): graduate school. 落ちる (おちる): to fall; here, to fail an exam."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"aoi", ja:"おばあちゃんが[心配]{しんぱい}じゃないわけじゃないよ。でも、それだけで来たわけでもない。", en:"It's not that I don't worry about Grandma. But it's not as if she was my only reason, either."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"cheska", ja:"…知ってた。四月から。", en:"...I knew. Since April."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"cheska", ja:"でも、あの夜、あおいは電話を[三回]{さんかい}かけて、雨の中を行ったでしょ。あれは[半分]{はんぶん}じゃなかったよ。", en:"But that night you rang three times, and then you went, in that rain. There was nothing half about that."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Aoi, read as lazy for six months by the person whose opinion she most wanted, has nothing clever to say. She has paid in first. Cheska doesn't pay back, not today."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Late October. The old horror films have stopped coming through the wall of Room 101. At four in the morning Cheska is at the kitchen table with the rain radar open, under a perfectly clear sky. Somebody comes down the hall in work boots, trying to be quiet, which has never been one of Rodrigo's skills."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"cheska", ja:"ロドリゴ？こんな時間に、どこへ行くの。", en:"Rodrigo? Where are you going at this hour?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"rodrigo", ja:"…仕事だ。つばめ通りの[裏]{うら}の[倉庫]{そうこ}を[片付]{かたづ}ける。朝までで一万円、[現金]{げんきん}で。", en:"...Work. Clearing out a warehouse behind Swallow Street. Ten thousand yen till morning, in cash.", gl:"裏 (うら): the back. 倉庫 (そうこ): a warehouse. 現金 (げんきん): cash."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"cheska", ja:"今週は、もう二十八時間[働]{はたら}いたでしょ。[留学生]{りゅうがくせい}は、[週]{しゅう}に二十八時間までだよ。", en:"You've already worked twenty-eight hours this week. Twenty-eight a week is the limit for an international student.", gl:"留学生 (りゅうがくせい): an international student."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"rodrigo", ja:"[書類]{しょるい}のない仕事だ。だれにも分からない。", en:"It's a job with no paperwork. Nobody will know.", gl:"書類 (しょるい): documents, paperwork."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"cheska", ja:"だれにも分からなくても、ルールは同じ。もし分かったら、ビザの[更新]{こうしん}ができなくなるかもしれないよ。", en:"Even if nobody knows, the rule is the same. And if it did come out, you might not be able to renew your visa.", gl:"更新 (こうしん): renewal."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"cheska", ja:"一万円のかわりに、日本のスタジオで[働]{はたら}くチャンスをなくすの？", en:"You'd give up your chance of working at a studio in Japan, in exchange for ten thousand yen?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"rodrigo", ja:"…金がないんだ。ふとんさえ買えない。", en:"...I've got no money. I can't even buy a futon.", gl:"金 (かね): money, said roughly."},
    {t:"narr", text:"His futon went out with the tatami. For five weeks he has slept on three floor cushions, and told the house that this is how a samurai sleeps."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"cheska", ja:"どうして言わなかったの。", en:"Why didn't you say?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"rodrigo", ja:"チェスカだって言わないじゃないか。雨が[降]{ふ}っていなくても、毎[晩]{ばん}、雨のレーダーを見ているのに。", en:"You don't say either, do you? You look at the rain radar every night, even when it isn't raining.", gl:"～だって: ～ too, even ～. ～じゃないか: *do you?*, pushing back. レーダー: radar."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"cheska", ja:"…私は[大丈夫]{だいじょうぶ}。", en:"...I'm fine."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Neither wanted to be noticed, and both have been. Rodrigo takes his boots off and makes hot chocolate instead. Cheska, who trades away every cooking turn, drinks two cups. By breakfast a form is taped to the door of Room 102: the university's emergency fund for students hit by the flood, with the boxes he would get wrong marked in pencil."},
    {t:"narr", text:"November brings the first real rain since. At one in the morning Aoi comes down for water and finds Cheska on the bottom stair, dressed, shoes on, a packed bag beside her."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"cheska", ja:"雨の音がするたびに、[目]{め}が[覚]{さ}めるの。気がつくと、ここにいる。", en:"Every time I hear rain, I wake up. And then I find I'm here.", gl:"目が覚める (めがさめる): to wake up. 気がつくと: before I know it."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"cheska", ja:"[大丈夫]{だいじょうぶ}なわけじゃない。でも、だめなわけでもないの。ただ、[眠]{ねむ}れないだけ。", en:"It's not that I'm fine. It's not that I'm falling apart, either. I just can't sleep.", gl:"眠る (ねむる): to sleep."},
    {t:"note", text:"大丈夫じゃない would have been an alarm. 大丈夫なわけじゃない is smaller and more exact: it takes back one conclusion, *so she must be fine*, and leaves everything else standing. Cheska has already said 大丈夫 twice this autumn. It is the first word most people learn for this and the last one they should be believed on."},
    {t:"narr", text:"It is the most she has said in seven weeks. The last time water came into a house Cheska lived in, she was sixteen. That is a long story, and Aoi doesn't ask for it tonight. She sits down on the stair."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"aoi", ja:"一人で起きていることはないよ。雨の夜は、だれかがいっしょに起きていればいいでしょ。", en:"There's no need to sit up on your own. On rainy nights, somebody can just sit up with you.", gl:"～ことはない: there is no need to ～."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Cheska begins to say that she couldn't ask that of anyone."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"aoi", ja:"あの夜、チェスカはみんなを学校まで歩かせたんだよ。一[晩]{ばん}くらい、だれかに起きていてもらっても、いいと思うけど。", en:"You walked the whole house up to that school. I'd say you're allowed to have someone sit up with you for a night or so.", gl:"一晩 (ひとばん): one night. ～くらい: ～ or so, ～ at least."},
    {t:"narr", text:"By the weekend the house app has a new row: 雨の夜, *rainy nights*. Kaito wrote it and Yến reviewed it, in four minutes. On the next wet night Kaito sits up pretending to revise, Cheska puts on a horror film from 1998, and he turns out to hold strong, wrong opinions about it. She sleeps six hours. The cat takes the packed bag."},
    {t:"cat", pose:"sleepy", alt:"The cat curled up asleep on Cheska's packed bag."},
    {t:"narr", text:"The city archive's basement flooded too. The work is called 資料レスキュー, document rescue: kitchen paper between the wet pages, and fans. Mrs Satō announced it at Sunday dinner, so the whole house is here. Toby, who reads old handwriting, has the ledger nobody else would touch."},
    {t:"plates", title:"The ledger", hint:"Read each line of the page, then tap it to check.", items:[
      {ja:"住居表示 新旧対照簿", ro:"じゅうきょひょうじ しんきゅうたいしょうぼ", who:"*Addresses, old and new, side by side.* 住居表示 is the modern system of numbering addresses. Many Japanese cities changed over to it in the 1960s, district by district, and kept a ledger like this one so that an old address could still be traced."},
      {ja:"昭和四十三年 四月一日 実施", ro:"しょうわ よんじゅうさんねん しがつ ついたち じっし", who:"*In force from 1 April, Shōwa 43.* 昭和 is the era name, and its forty-third year is 1968. 実施 (じっし) is putting something into effect."},
      {ja:"旧：川南 一二六番地", ro:"きゅう：かわみなみ ひゃくにじゅうろく ばんち", who:"*Old: lot 126, Kawaminami.* 旧 marks what something used to be, as in 旧市街, the old town."},
      {ja:"新：川南町二丁目 四番九号", ro:"しん：かわみなみちょう にちょうめ よんばん きゅうごう", who:"*New: 4-9, Kawaminami-chō 2-chōme.* From that day there was no such place as 126 Kawaminami."},
      {ja:"世帯主：村井 （転出）", ro:"せたいぬし：むらい （てんしゅつ）", who:"*Head of household: Murai.* Beside the name, in a clerk's pencil, 転出: *moved away*."}]},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"toby", ja:"「[川南]{かわみなみ}、一二六[番地]{ばんち}」…。あおい、この[住所]{じゅうしょ}、どこかで見なかったっけ。", en:"\"Kawaminami, lot 126\"... Aoi, haven't we seen this address somewhere?", gl:"番地 (ばんち): a lot number in an address. ～っけ: *didn't we?*, said when you are trying to remember."},
    {t:"line", mood:"yay", who:"aoi", ja:"見た。[物置]{ものおき}のかんの手紙。[全部]{ぜんぶ}、この[住所]{じゅうしょ}だった。", en:"We have. The letters in the tin in the storeroom. Every one of them had this address.", gl:"物置 (ものおき): a storeroom. かん: a tin."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Mrs Satō comes over from the next table and puts on her glasses."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"fumiko", ja:"[村井]{むらい}は、私の[結婚]{けっこん}する前の名前です。…父ですね。", en:"Murai was my name before I married. ...That's my father.", gl:"結婚 (けっこん)する: to get married."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"fumiko", ja:"この年の春に、うちは町の[反対側]{はんたいがわ}に[引]{ひ}っ[越]{こ}したんです。同じ春に、[住所]{じゅうしょ}の書き方まで[変]{か}わったんですね。", en:"That spring we moved to the other side of town. And the same spring, it seems, even the way of writing addresses changed.", gl:"反対側 (はんたいがわ): the opposite side. 引っ越す (ひっこす): to move house."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"fumiko", ja:"四月からは、「[川南]{かわみなみ}126」に手紙を出しても、[届]{とど}かなかったでしょうね。新しい[住所]{じゅうしょ}は、手紙で知らせたはずなんですけど。", en:"From that April, a letter posted to \"126 Kawaminami\" wouldn't have arrived, I suppose. I'm sure I wrote and told her the new address, though."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"fumiko", ja:"手紙というのは、[住所]{じゅうしょ}が[違]{ちが}うと、どんなに待っても[届]{とど}かないものですから。", en:"A letter with the wrong address never arrives, however long you wait. That is how letters are.", gl:"どんなに～ても: however much ～. ～ものだ: that is the nature of things."},
    {t:"narr", text:"She has waited fifty-eight years. She lays a dry sheet under the wet page, smooths it flat, and goes back to her own table. Aoi photographs the page."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Other things happened that November. The city asked Dr Amoako's lab for a page carrying its alerts in more languages. Yến built one in a week, with text in six; Siti said, kindly, that her dormitory doesn't read much, it sends voice messages, and Yến began again. Mariya had an interview. Toby took a call from home out among the leeks, and told nobody."},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u10-x1", type:"mcq", q:"On the stairs Cheska says [大丈夫]{だいじょうぶ}なわけじゃない。でも、だめなわけでもないの。 What is she telling Aoi?", options:[
      {t:"She isn't simply fine, and she isn't in a terrible state either; the truth is somewhere in between", ok:true, why:"Right. ～わけではない denies a conclusion without claiming the opposite. She takes back *so I must be fine*, and then takes back *so I must be falling apart* as well. What is left is ただ、[眠]{ねむ}れないだけ."},
      {t:"She is completely fine, as she said before", why:"That was [大丈夫]{だいじょうぶ}, on the bench and in the kitchen. ～なわけじゃない takes that conclusion back."},
      {t:"There is no reason for Aoi to be fine", why:"わけ can mean *reason*, but ～わけではない is a set pattern: *it isn't that ～*. And she is talking about herself."},
      {t:"She can't cope at all", why:"She rules that out too: だめなわけでもない. も adds a second thing that isn't the case."}]}},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u10-x2", type:"mcq", q:"At the counter Aoi says [申請]{しんせい}に[参]{まい}りました, and Mr Matsumoto asks お写真はお持ちですか. What is each of them doing?", options:[
      {t:"Each lowers their own action and raises the other person's", ok:true, why:"Right. [参]{まい}る is the humble *come*, for Aoi's own action. お持ちですか is the respectful *do you have?*, for the visitors. Mr Matsumoto does the same with his own side: [申]{もう}します, [伺]{うかが}う, おりました."},
      {t:"Aoi is raising herself, because she is the customer", why:"Nobody raises themselves in keigo. [参]{まい}る lowers the speaker's own coming and going."},
      {t:"Both verbs are respectful, about Mr Matsumoto", why:"[参]{まい}りました is about Aoi's own coming, and お持ちですか is about what the visitors have."},
      {t:"Mr Matsumoto is being humble about his own photographs", why:"The photographs are Cheska's. お + [持]{も}ち + です is the respectful pattern for the other person's action or state."}]}},
    {t:"lang", items:["Even if: お送りになっても、読めなければ… (Cheska), だれにも分からなくても、ルールは同じ (Cheska), 雨が[降]{ふ}っていなくても (Rodrigo), どんなに待っても[届]{とど}かない (Mrs Satō). ～ても grants the first half and says the second half holds anyway.", "Not exactly: [届]{とど}いたわけではありません, [責]{せ}めているわけではないんです, [大丈夫]{だいじょうぶ}なわけじゃない. Aoi's [心配]{しんぱい}じゃないわけじゃない has two negatives, so it means *I do worry*, said carefully.", "Keigo at the counter runs both ways. Mr Matsumoto's own actions are humble ([申]{もう}します, [伺]{うかが}う, お送りいたしました, おりました), and the visitors' are respectful (お持ちですか, おっしゃる, いらっしゃった). Aoi and Cheska do the same from their side ([参]{まい}りました, お送りになりました). Cheska gets angry without dropping a single form."]},
    {t:"reflect", q:"Aoi says 一人で起きていることはないよ, and the house adds a row to its app. When someone you know keeps saying [大丈夫]{だいじょうぶ}, what kind of help have you found they can accept?"}
  ]},
  {unit:"e3u11", n:11, title:"Winter visitors", month:"December–January", level:"N3", parts:[
    {t:"narr", text:"*Previously at Kamome House:* The water came twelve centimetres over the floor and went again. Cheska stopped saying she was fine, and the house app gained a row for rainy nights. At the city archive a wet ledger showed why, after April 1968, no letter to 126 Kawaminami could have arrived."},
    {t:"narr", text:"There is a shelf by the stairs at Kamome House. Leave something broken on it, and a few days later it is back, mended, with no note. Everybody knows who does it. Nobody has ever said so, and that is the arrangement."},
    {t:"narr", text:"The first heavy snow comes in the second week of December. At six that morning Mr Satō crosses the garden with Mariya's umbrella, which opens again, and his feet go from under him on the three stone steps at the front door. Kaito, coming home from the night shift, finds him sitting in the snow, unable to get up and extremely annoyed about it."},
    {t:"plates", title:"On the ward", hint:"Read each sign, then tap it to check.", items:[
      {ja:"整形外科 病棟", ro:"せいけいげか びょうとう", who:"*Orthopaedic ward.* 整形外科 is the department for bones and joints, and 病棟 is a hospital ward."},
      {ja:"面会時間：午後二時から七時まで", ro:"めんかいじかん：ごご にじから しちじまで", who:"*Visiting hours: 2 to 7 p.m.* 面会 is seeing someone face to face. It is the word hospitals use for a visit."},
      {ja:"転倒注意", ro:"てんとうちゅうい", who:"*Beware of falls.* 転 is to tumble, 倒 is to fall over, and 注意 is care. The card hangs above Mr Satō's bed. He considers it late."},
      {ja:"退院予定日：未定", ro:"たいいんよていび：みてい", who:"*Planned discharge date: not yet decided.* 退院 is leaving hospital, the opposite of 入院. 未 means *not yet*, so 未定 is undecided for now."}]},
    {t:"narr", text:"A cracked bone low in his back: a corset, no operation, about two weeks. It is the city hospital, where his daughter Megumi nurses two floors down. On the third day his first visitor is nine years old and has come straight from school."},
    {t:"line", mood:"yay", who:"sota", ja:"おじいちゃん、にゃん[助]{すけ}は元気だよ。毎日ぼくがごはんをあげてるから、[安心]{あんしん}して。", en:"Grandad, Nyansuke's fine. I'm feeding her every day, so don't worry.", gl:"安心 (あんしん)する: to stop worrying, to feel safe."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"shoichi", ja:"にゃん[太郎]{たろう}だ。", en:"Nyantarō."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"sota", ja:"にゃん[助]{すけ}だってば。", en:"It's Nyansuke, I keep telling you.", gl:"～ってば: *I'm telling you*, said when the other person isn't listening."},
    {t:"narr", text:"This has been going on since Sōta could talk. The next visitor is Kaito, with a paper bag."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"kaito", ja:"あの、[棚]{たな}にラジオが[置]{お}いてあったんですけど。音が出なくて。", en:"Um, there was a radio left on the shelf. It isn't making any sound.", gl:"棚 (たな): a shelf. 置く (おく): to put, to leave."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Nobody has ever told Mr Satō to his face that the shelf is his. Strictly speaking, Kaito still hasn't."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"shoichi", ja:"…中を見たか。", en:"...Did you look inside?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"kaito", ja:"見ました。[線]{せん}が一本、[外]{はず}れていました。", en:"I did. One wire had come off.", gl:"線 (せん): a wire, a line. 外れる (はずれる): to come off."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"shoichi", ja:"はんだは、[机]{つくえ}の右の[引]{ひ}き出しだ。[熱]{あつ}いから、ゆっくりやれ。", en:"The solder's in the right-hand drawer of the desk. It's hot, so take it slowly.", gl:"はんだ: solder. 引き出し (ひきだし): a drawer. 熱い (あつい): hot to the touch. やれ: the blunt command form of やる."},
    {t:"narr", text:"That is the entire handover. Megumi has looked in on her break, still in uniform, in time to hear it."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"megumi", ja:"[以心伝心]{いしんでんしん}ね。うちの[男]{おとこ}の人は、[大事]{だいじ}なことほど[言葉]{ことば}にしないんだから。", en:"Mind to mind, I see. The men in this family: the more something matters, the less they put it into words.", gl:"以心伝心 (いしんでんしん): understanding each other without words. 大事 (だいじ): important."},
    {t:"narr", text:"The family's other man is in the corridor. Hiroyuki works in a city four hours away by train, and came on the first one. He still has his coat on, and a brochure for a block of flats in his hand."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"hiroyuki", ja:"家を[売]{う}って、うちの近くのマンションに[移]{うつ}ればいいんだ。エレベーターがあるし、[病院]{びょういん}も近い。[雪]{ゆき}だって、ほとんど[降]{ふ}らない。", en:"They should sell the house and move into a flat near us. There's a lift, and a hospital close by. It hardly even snows.", gl:"売る (うる): to sell. マンション: a block of flats. 移る (うつる): to move."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"megumi", ja:"お父さんの[顔]{かお}を見る前に、もうその話？", en:"You haven't even seen Dad's face yet, and we're on to that already?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"hiroyuki", ja:"[洪水]{こうずい}の[次]{つぎ}は[骨折]{こっせつ}だぞ。[不安]{ふあん}で、夜も[眠]{ねむ}れない。毎[晩]{ばん}電話しても、母さんは「[大丈夫]{だいじょうぶ}」しか言わないし。", en:"First a flood, now a broken bone. I'm so worried I can't sleep. I ring every night, and all Mum ever says is \"we're fine\".", gl:"洪水 (こうずい): a flood. 骨折 (こっせつ): a broken bone. 不安 (ふあん): anxious, uneasy."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"megumi", ja:"毎週ここへ来て、[薬]{くすり}を[数]{かぞ}えて、あの[階段]{かいだん}を見ていらいらしているのは、私だよ。お兄ちゃんが来るのは、年に[二回]{にかい}でしょ。", en:"I'm the one who comes every week, counts the pills, and looks at those stairs and frets. You come twice a year.", gl:"薬 (くすり): medicine. いらいらする: to be on edge, irritated."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"megumi", ja:"それなのに、[大事]{だいじ}なことを[決]{き}めるときだけ、[長男]{ちょうなん}の[顔]{かお}をするんだから。", en:"And yet the moment there's something important to decide, you turn up as the eldest son.", gl:"それなのに: and yet. 長男 (ちょうなん): the eldest son. ～の顔をする: to act the part of ～."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"hiroyuki", ja:"…[遠]{とお}くにいるから、[余計]{よけい}にこわいんだよ。", en:"...It's because I'm far away that it frightens me all the more.", gl:"余計に (よけいに): all the more."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Neither of them is wrong, which is what makes it a family argument. For two weeks the things left on the shelf go on coming back mended: a little less neatly, and once with a note of apology, which is against the rules. The cat, whom Kaito calls 師匠, *master*, watches every joint. On the twenty-sixth Mr Satō comes home with a corset and a stick."},
    {t:"cat", pose:"curious", alt:"The cat looking up with her ears forward, watching Kaito work."},
    {t:"narr", text:"A soba shop's busiest night is New Year's Eve, when the whole town eats noodles to see the old year out. This year, for the first time in his life, Kaito wasn't behind the counter. On the second of January, with the shop shut for the holiday, his father comes down from the mountains with a bag of buckwheat flour and no explanation, and finds his son making soba for twenty in somebody else's kitchen."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Twenty means the Satōs, their children and Sōta, the family from the Nepali restaurant on Swallow Street, Chiyo, Siti, seven residents, and one silent man at the far end. When everyone has a bowl, Mrs Satō puts her chopsticks down."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"fumiko", ja:"食べながらでいいので、聞いてください。この家を[売]{う}るか、[売]{う}らないか。どちらも[一長一短]{いっちょういったん}で、[家族]{かぞく}だけでは[決]{き}められません。", en:"Do go on eating, but listen, please. Whether to sell this house or not. Each has its good and bad points, and the family can't decide it alone.", gl:"一長一短 (いっちょういったん): having both good points and bad points. 家族 (かぞく): a family."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"fumiko", ja:"ここは[皆]{みな}さんの家でもあります。[遠慮]{えんりょ}しないで、[意見]{いけん}を聞かせてください。", en:"This is your house too. Don't hold back; let us hear what you think.", gl:"遠慮 (えんりょ)する: to hold back out of politeness. 意見 (いけん): an opinion."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Toby first slept in this house at fifteen, on a school exchange. He is also a man who tells people what they want to hear, and at this table two people want opposite things."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"toby", ja:"…[売]{う}らないでほしいです。十五のとき、[初]{はじ}めてここに[泊]{と}めてもらいました。今も、ここがぼくの日本のうちです。", en:"...I'd like you not to sell. I first stayed here when I was fifteen. It's still my home in Japan.", gl:"泊める (とめる): to put someone up for the night."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"hiroyuki", ja:"気持ちはうれしいです。でも、父はもう[階段]{かいだん}を[上]{のぼ}れません。それに、ここは水も来る[所]{ところ}です。", en:"I'm glad you feel that way. But my father can't climb stairs any more. And on top of that, this is a place where the water comes.", gl:"上る (のぼる): to climb. それに: on top of that."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"cheska", ja:"水が[危険]{きけん}なのは[本当]{ほんとう}です。でも、水は来る前に[警報]{けいほう}が出ます。[階段]{かいだん}と[雪]{ゆき}は、何も知らせてくれません。", en:"The water is a real danger. But before water comes, there's a warning. Stairs and snow don't tell you anything.", gl:"危険 (きけん): danger. 警報 (けいほう): a warning, an alert."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"aoi", ja:"[物置]{ものおき}は[一階]{いっかい}ですよね。あそこを[部屋]{へや}にすれば、[階段]{かいだん}は一[段]{だん}も使わなくていいんじゃないですか。", en:"The storeroom is on the ground floor, isn't it? If that were made into rooms, nobody would need to use a single stair.", gl:"物置 (ものおき): a storeroom. 一段も～ない: not even one step."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"shoichi", ja:"[柱]{はしら}はしっかりしている。[床]{ゆか}を[直]{なお}して[段差]{だんさ}をなくせば、[住]{す}める。", en:"The posts are sound. Mend the floor and take out the steps, and it can be lived in.", gl:"柱 (はしら): a post, a pillar. 床 (ゆか): the floor. 段差 (だんさ): a step, a difference in level."},
    {t:"narr", text:"He has plainly measured it already, probably in October. Megumi puts her bowl down."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"megumi", ja:"[賛成]{さんせい}したい。でも、[正直]{しょうじき}に言うね。私は、これ[以上]{いじょう}は[無理]{むり}。[夜勤]{やきん}もあるし、[颯太]{そうた}もいるし。", en:"I'd like to agree. But I'll be honest. I can't do any more than I'm doing. I've got night shifts, and I've got Sōta.", gl:"賛成 (さんせい): agreement. 正直 (しょうじき)に: honestly. 無理 (むり): impossible, too much. 夜勤 (やきん): a night shift."},
    {t:"narr", text:"It is the first time she has said 無理 in front of her mother. Her brother looks at her for some time."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"hiroyuki", ja:"…[恵]{めぐみ}が毎週来てくれるから、おれは[遠]{とお}くで[働]{はたら}けるんだよな。一度も、ありがとうと言っていなかった。", en:"...It's because you come every week that I can work so far away, isn't it. I've never once said thank you."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"megumi", ja:"…毎[晩]{ばん}の電話、お母さんは[楽]{たの}しみにしてるよ。私も、言っていなかったけど。", en:"...Mum looks forward to that call every night, you know. Not that I ever told you, either.", gl:"楽しみにする (たのしみにする): to look forward to."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"aoi", ja:"あの。[家賃]{やちん}を少し安くしていただけるなら、[管理人]{かんりにん}の仕事は私がやります。[家賃]{やちん}を[集]{あつ}めたり、[修理]{しゅうり}を[頼]{たの}んだり、ごみの[当番]{とうばん}を[決]{き}めたり。", en:"Um. If you could take a little off my rent, I'll do the manager's work. Collecting the rent, calling in repairs, the rubbish rota.", gl:"家賃 (やちん): rent. 管理人 (かんりにん): a building manager, a caretaker. 修理 (しゅうり): a repair. 当番 (とうばん): a turn on a rota."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"aoi", ja:"[親切]{しんせつ}で言っているわけではありません。[家賃]{やちん}のためです。", en:"I'm not saying it to be kind. It's for the rent.", gl:"親切 (しんせつ): kindness."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Nobody at the table believes this, and the cat doesn't look convinced either."},
    {t:"cat", pose:"smug", alt:"The cat sitting by the low table, looking pleased with herself."},
    {t:"line", mood:"yay", who:"fumiko", ja:"[一石二鳥]{いっせきにちょう}ですね。主人は[階段]{かいだん}を使わない。私は仕事が[減]{へ}る。", en:"Two birds with one stone, then. My husband stays off the stairs, and I have less to do.", gl:"一石二鳥 (いっせきにちょう): one stone, two birds. 減る (へる): to get less."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"hiroyuki", ja:"…もう[階段]{かいだん}を[上]{のぼ}らないと[約束]{やくそく}してくれるなら、[反対]{はんたい}はしないよ。", en:"...If you'll promise never to climb those stairs again, I won't oppose it.", gl:"約束 (やくそく): a promise. 反対 (はんたい): opposition, the opposite of 賛成."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"shoichi", ja:"[約束]{やくそく}する。[二階]{にかい}の[電球]{でんきゅう}は、[海斗]{かいと}に[任]{まか}せた。", en:"I promise. The light bulbs upstairs I've handed over to Kaito.", gl:"電球 (でんきゅう): a light bulb. 任せる (まかせる): to leave something in someone's hands."},
    {t:"narr", text:"So that is decided: the house stays, the storeroom becomes a flat with no steps in it, and Aoi becomes the manager. From the far end of the table comes the first word Kaito's father has spoken since he sat down."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"kuze", ja:"…お[代]{か}わり。", en:"...Another bowl.", gl:"お代わり (おかわり): a second helping."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Afterwards there are twenty bowls. Kaito washes. His father, without being asked, dries."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"kuze", ja:"水が少し多い。[次]{つぎ}は[減]{へ}らせ。", en:"A touch too much water. Use less next time.", gl:"減らす (へらす): to reduce."},
    {t:"narr", text:"A man does not correct the noodles of someone he has given up on. Kaito knows it, and it gets him as far as his next sentence."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"kaito", ja:"父さん。おれ、プログラムを書く仕事がしたい。でも、そばを[打]{う}つのも[好]{す}きなんだ。どっちも[本当]{ほんとう}。", en:"Dad. I want to write programs for a living. But I love making soba too. Both of those are true.", gl:"そばを打つ (うつ): to make soba by hand."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"kuze", ja:"店は、ばあちゃんの[介護]{かいご}を[支]{ささ}えている。町には、もう[他]{ほか}に食べる[所]{ところ}がない。「[好]{す}きにしろ」とは、[簡単]{かんたん}には言えん。", en:"The shop pays for your grandmother's care. There's nowhere else left in town to eat. I can't just say \"do as you like\".", gl:"介護 (かいご): nursing care. 支える (ささえる): to support. 言えん: 言えない, in an older man's speech."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"kaito", ja:"分かってる。", en:"I know."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"kuze", ja:"お前の名前の「海」はな、おれが[若]{わか}いころ行きたかった[所]{ところ}だ。山を出て、海の見える町で[働]{はたら}くつもりだった。[結局]{けっきょく}、行かなかったが。", en:"The \"sea\" in your name is where I wanted to go when I was young. I meant to leave the mountains and work in a town where you could see the sea. I never went, in the end.", gl:"お前 (おまえ): *you*, from a father to a son. 若い (わかい): young. 結局 (けっきょく): in the end."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"kaito", ja:"…[初]{はじ}めて聞いた。", en:"...That's the first I've heard of it."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"kuze", ja:"だから、お前が海の町にいるのは、[悪]{わる}い気はしない。店のことは[未定]{みてい}だ。春に、また話そう。", en:"So having you in a town by the sea doesn't sit badly with me. The shop is undecided. We'll talk again in spring.", gl:"悪い気はしない: I don't mind it; it feels rather good. 未定 (みてい): not yet decided."},
    {t:"note", text:"Japanese has four small kanji that go in front of a word to say *not*: 不, 無, 非 and 未. Megumi's 無理 closes something: there is no way. Hiroyuki's 不安 is a lack: no peace of mind. 未定 says only *not yet*. Of the four, 未 is the one with a future in it."},
    {t:"narr", text:"He takes the last train back up the mountain. In Room 102 Rodrigo is reading an email from an animation studio for the fifteenth time, having so far told only the cat. And in the storeroom, by torchlight, a man in a corset is measuring a doorway. He did not use the stairs to get there."},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u11-x1", type:"mcq", q:"The card above Mr Satō's bed says [転倒注意]{てんとうちゅうい}. What is it telling people?", options:[
      {t:"Take care: there is a risk of falling over", ok:true, why:"Right. [転]{てん} is to tumble, [倒]{とう} is to fall over, and 注意 is care. Hospitals hang it by the beds of patients who are unsteady on their feet."},
      {t:"No visitors without permission", why:"Visits are [面会]{めんかい}, as in [面会]{めんかい}時間. This card is about the patient's balance."},
      {t:"The patient is about to change wards", why:"[転]{てん} does mean *move* or *transfer* in some words, but here it joins [倒]{とう}, to fall over: [転倒]{てんとう} is a fall."},
      {t:"Take care: the floor is being cleaned", why:"There is nothing about cleaning or floors in these four kanji: tumble, fall over, and 注意."}]}},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u11-x2", type:"mcq", q:"Mrs Satō says [一石二鳥]{いっせきにちょう}ですね. What are her two birds?", options:[
      {t:"Her husband stays off the stairs, and she has less work", ok:true, why:"Right. She names them herself: 主人は[階段]{かいだん}を使わない。私は仕事が[減]{へ}る。 One stone (一石), two birds (二鳥): the ground-floor flat and a manager, got with one decision."},
      {t:"Selling the house and buying a flat", why:"That was Hiroyuki's plan in the hospital corridor. The idiom comes after the family has moved away from it."},
      {t:"Aoi gets cheaper rent and the cat gets fed", why:"Aoi does ask for her [家賃]{やちん} to come down, but Mrs Satō's two gains are her husband's and her own."},
      {t:"Everyone has a different opinion", why:"That would be [十人十色]{じゅうにんといろ}: ten people, ten colours."}]}},
    {t:"lang", items:["Four-kanji idioms can often be read from their parts. [以心伝心]{いしんでんしん}: by the heart (以心), pass on the heart ([伝心]{でんしん}). [一長一短]{いっちょういったん}: one long, one short, so a good point and a bad one. [一石二鳥]{いっせきにちょう}: one stone, two birds.", "Three ways of *not*: [不安]{ふあん} (no peace of mind), [無理]{むり} (no way; too much to ask) and [未定]{みてい} (not decided yet). And two pairs of opposites from this episode: 入院 and [退院]{たいいん}, [賛成]{さんせい} and [反対]{はんたい}.", "Family words change with the listener. Inside the family Megumi says お父さん, お母さん and お兄ちゃん. Speaking to the residents, Hiroyuki calls the same man 父, and Mrs Satō calls him 主人: plain words for your own family in front of other people."]},
    {t:"reflect", q:"Megumi stayed in Shioura and Hiroyuki left, and each has been carrying something the other hadn't thanked them for. In your family, or your house, who does the visiting and who does the worrying from far away?"}
  ]},
  {unit:"e3u12", n:12, title:"Letters in spring", month:"February–March", level:"N3", parts:[
    {t:"narr", text:"*Previously at Kamome House:* Mr Satō fell on the snowy front steps and spent two weeks in hospital. At New Year the family asked the house what it thought, and decided: no sale, a flat without steps where the storeroom is, and Aoi as manager. Kaito's father asked for a second bowl."},
    {t:"narr", text:"February. Two carpenters are taking up the storeroom floor, and Mr Satō supervises from a kitchen chair in the garden, in a corset and three coats, giving advice that is correct and not wanted. The trail took all winter: a date in a ledger, Toby's old school, a local history society in Australia. In January a woman of seventy-five wrote back. Her name is Lorraine. Now there is a parcel."},
    {t:"plates", title:"The envelope", hint:"Read what is written and stamped on it, then tap to check.", items:[
      {ja:"汐浦市 川南 126", ro:"しおうらし かわみなみ 126", who:"The address, copied stroke by careful stroke, in the same hand as every envelope in the tin."},
      {ja:"あて所に尋ねあたりません", ro:"あてどころに たずねあたりません", who:"*Not found at this address.* A post-office stamp, in purple. あて所 is the address a letter is sent to, and 尋ねあたる is to ask around and find. Returned post in Japan still carries these words."},
      {ja:"差出人に返送", ro:"さしだしにんに へんそう", who:"*Return to sender.* 差出人 is the person who sent it, and 返送 is sending something back."},
      {ja:"昭和四十三年 五月", ro:"しょうわ よんじゅうさんねん ごがつ", who:"*May, Shōwa 43*: 1968, the month after 126 Kawaminami stopped existing. The envelope has never been opened."}]},
    {t:"narr", text:"Three letters, kept for nearly fifty-nine years by a woman who could never quite throw them away. Mrs Satō slits the first with the fruit knife. The handwriting defeats her, so Toby reads it out, putting it into Japanese as he goes."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"toby", ja:"「フミコへ。お元気ですか。一月に手紙を出しましたが、まだお[返事]{へんじ}が来ません。」", en:"\"Dear Fumiko, how are you? I wrote in January, but there's been no answer yet.\"", gl:"返事 (へんじ): a reply."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"toby", ja:"「病気ではないかと[心配]{しんぱい}しています。それとも、私が何か[失礼]{しつれい}なことを書いたのでしょうか。」", en:"\"I'm worried that you may be ill. Or did I write something rude?\"", gl:"それとも: or else. 失礼 (しつれい): rude, impolite."},
    {t:"narr", text:"The third is dated December 1968."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"toby", ja:"「これが[最後]{さいご}の手紙になるかもしれません。でも、あなたの[住所]{じゅうしょ}は、もう何も見ないで書けるようになりました。」", en:"\"This may be my last letter. But I can write your address now without looking at anything.\"", gl:"最後 (さいご): the last."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Nobody says anything. Mariya has stopped pretending to make tea."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"fumiko", ja:"…「[失礼]{しつれい}なこと」を書いたのは、私のほうだと思っていました。", en:"...I always thought I was the one who had written something rude."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"fumiko", ja:"[引]{ひ}っ[越]{こ}す前に出した手紙で、あの子の漢字の書き[順]{じゅん}を[直]{なお}したんです。「さんずいは上から書きましょう」と。", en:"In the letter I sent before we moved, I corrected the stroke order of her kanji. \"Let's write the water radical from the top.\"", gl:"書き順 (かきじゅん): stroke order. 直す (なおす): to correct. さんずい: the three-stroke water radical on the left of 汐 and 浦."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"mariya", ja:"え、それで[怒]{おこ}らせたと思っていたんですか。五十九年も？", en:"What, and you thought that had made her angry? For fifty-nine years?", gl:"怒らせる (おこらせる): to make someone angry."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"fumiko", ja:"ですから、それからは、人を[直]{なお}すのは[一回]{いっかい}だけにしているんです。", en:"Which is why, ever since, I have only corrected a person once."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"toby", ja:"その手紙、たぶん[向]{む}こうには[届]{とど}いていませんよ。新しい[住所]{じゅうしょ}といっしょに。", en:"That letter probably never got there, you know. Along with the new address.", gl:"向こう (むこう): the other side; here, Lorraine's end."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Mrs Satō writes her answer in Japanese first, in pencil, and reads it to the kitchen the way she once read model compositions to a class. Mariya will put it into English."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"fumiko", ja:"「ロレインさんへ。お手紙は、五十九年かかって[届]{とど}きました。ありがとうございます。」", en:"\"Dear Lorraine, your letters have arrived. They took fifty-nine years. Thank you.\""},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"fumiko", ja:"「あの春、私の家は[引]{ひ}っ[越]{こ}しをしました。その上、町の[住所]{じゅうしょ}の書き方も[変]{か}わりました。新しい[住所]{じゅうしょ}を書いた手紙は、あなたに[届]{とど}かなかったようです。」", en:"\"That spring my family moved house. On top of that, the town changed the way its addresses were written. The letter in which I gave you my new address seems never to have reached you.\"", gl:"その上 (そのうえ): on top of that."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"fumiko", ja:"「私は長い間、あなたが書くのをやめたのだと思っていました。しかし、やめた人はだれもいなかったのです。」", en:"\"For a long time I believed that you had stopped writing. But nobody had stopped.\"", gl:"しかし: however, but (written style)."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"fumiko", ja:"「つまり、[悪]{わる}かったのは、私でもあなたでもなく、[住所]{じゅうしょ}でした。」", en:"\"In short, the one at fault was neither you nor me. It was the address.\"", gl:"つまり: in short, in other words."},
    {t:"line", mood:"yay", who:"fumiko", ja:"「今度は、メールアドレスも書いておきます。お[返事]{へんじ}をお待ちしています。[文子]{ふみこ}」", en:"\"This time I am adding my email address as well. I look forward to your reply. Fumiko\""},
    {t:"narr", text:"March. Lorraine's granddaughter has arranged a video call. The tablet is propped against the rice cooker, and Mrs Satō is in her good cardigan. Mariya sits beside her to interpret. She writes English beautifully and speaks it as little as she can, except on Thursdays, with Toby. On the screen a white-haired woman leans in close. *Fumiko? Is that really you? Goodness. You've got old.*"},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"mariya", ja:"えーと…「[文子]{ふみこ}さん、[本当]{ほんとう}にあなたですか。年を[取]{と}りましたね」とおっしゃっています。", en:"Um... She says, \"Fumiko, is it really you? You've got old.\"", gl:"えーと: *um*, said while you find the words. 年を取る (としをとる): to grow old. ～とおっしゃっています: the respectful *she says ～*."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Mariya thought about softening it and, to her credit, hasn't."},
    {t:"line", mood:"yay", who:"fumiko", ja:"「あなたもね」と[伝]{つた}えてください。", en:"Please tell her: \"So have you.\"", gl:"伝える (つたえる): to pass on, to tell."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"fumiko", ja:"それから…「お[久]{ひさ}しぶりです」と。", en:"And then... \"Ohisashiburi desu.\"", gl:"お久しぶりです: what you say to someone you haven't seen for some time."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Two kitchens are laughing at *so have you*. The next one is harder. Mariya's whole degree is still ahead of her, and she already knows that English has nothing built for this. *It's been a while*, she says. Lorraine has to take her glasses off."},
    {t:"note", text:"お久しぶりです doesn't say how long. It leaves the number out and lets the two people supply it, which is why the same four beats will do for three weeks or for fifty-nine years. An interpreter's English has to pick a size. Mariya picked the smallest one, and she was right."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"mariya", ja:"「何か[失礼]{しつれい}なことを書いたのだと、ずっと思っていた」そうです。あのー、それで、手紙はどうしても[捨]{す}てられなかった、と。", en:"She says she always thought she had written something rude. Er, and so she could never bring herself to throw the letters away.", gl:"あのー: *er*, a filler. どうしても～ない: can't possibly ～. 捨てる (すてる): to throw away."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"fumiko", ja:"私も同じです、と…あ、いえ。それは、[自分]{じぶん}で言います。", en:"Tell her it was the same for... oh, no. That one I'll say myself.", gl:"自分で (じぶんで): by myself."},
    {t:"narr", text:"She sits up as she must have sat at sixteen and says it in English, each word on its own: *I thought you were angry. I corrected your kanji.* It takes Lorraine a moment; that letter never reached her. *Well, go on, then*, she says. *Correct it now.* She holds a sheet of paper up to the camera."},
    {t:"line", mood:"yay", who:"mariya", ja:"「じゃあ、今[直]{なお}して」って。あ、紙を見せていらっしゃいます。「[汐浦]{しおうら}」って書いてありますよ！", en:"She says, \"Then correct it now.\" Oh, she's showing us a piece of paper. It says \"Shioura\"!"},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"fumiko", ja:"…[上手]{じょうず}です。[直]{なお}す[所]{ところ}はありません、と[伝]{つた}えてください。", en:"...It is well written. Please tell her there is nothing to correct."},
    {t:"narr", text:"This is not quite true. The water radicals were drawn from the bottom up; you can tell from how the strokes land. But Mrs Satō corrected them once already, fifty-nine years ago, in a letter that never arrived, and once is her limit. Lorraine says something else, and Mariya goes pink."},
    {t:"line", mood:"oops", who:"mariya", ja:"あの…今のは、[訳]{やく}さなくてもいいですか。私のことなので。", en:"Um... may I not translate that one? It's about me.", gl:"訳す (やくす): to translate."},
    {t:"line", mood:"tip", who:"fumiko", ja:"[訳]{やく}してください。[全部]{ぜんぶ}[伝]{つた}えるのが、[通訳]{つうやく}の仕事でしょう。", en:"Translate it, please. Passing on all of it is an interpreter's job, I believe.", gl:"通訳 (つうやく): interpreting; an interpreter."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"mariya", ja:"…「英語がお[上手]{じょうず}ですね」とおっしゃっています。[自分]{じぶん}で言うと、はずかしいんですけど…。", en:"...She says, \"Your English is very good.\" It's embarrassing, saying it myself...", gl:"はずかしい: embarrassing. ～んですけど…: an unfinished sentence that leaves the rest unsaid."},
    {t:"narr", text:"She has been speaking English for twenty minutes without noticing. It is easier to be brave on someone else's behalf. *Write to me*, Lorraine says at the end. *On paper.*"},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"fumiko", ja:"書きます。今度は[住所]{じゅうしょ}を[三回]{さんかい}[確]{たし}かめてから出します、と[伝]{つた}えてください。", en:"I will. Please tell her that this time I shall check the address three times before I post it.", gl:"確かめる (たしかめる): to check, to make sure."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Late March. The flat smells of new wood and has a ramp where it might have had a step. Nobody's year has finished; each of them has a next thing. Rodrigo has a contract offer from a studio and an application in to change his visa, which is a question, not an answer. Yến has the offer she came for, as a bridge engineer: the person who stands between a software team in Vietnam and its clients in Japan. No bridges are involved. Kaito is going home for the holidays to work in the shop, and taking his laptop. The city's alert project meets on Tuesdays, led by Aoi and Yến, and Cheska sits at the side of the table on purpose. Aoi's job applications this spring are all addressed to Shioura. On Swallow Street last year's poster is back in the tea-shop window, with one date painted over. And in the vegetable patch Toby is digging while Mariya watches him dig."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"toby", ja:"きのう、うちに電話したよ。「[大丈夫]{だいじょうぶ}」って言うのは、もうやめた。父の病気のことも、ちゃんと聞いた。", en:"I rang home yesterday. I've stopped saying \"everything's fine\". And I asked properly about Dad's illness."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"mariya", ja:"…じゃあ、帰るの？", en:"...So are you going back?"},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"toby", ja:"まだ分からない。まりやは？[留学]{りゅうがく}、[受]{う}かったんでしょ。行くの？", en:"I don't know yet. What about you? You got the exchange place, didn't you? Are you going?", gl:"留学 (りゅうがく): study abroad. 受かる (うかる): to pass, to be accepted."},
    {t:"line", mood:"sleepy", who:"mariya", ja:"まだ分からない。行ったら、[島]{しま}を[捨]{す}てるみたいで…。[返事]{へんじ}のしめ切りは、金曜日なんだけど。", en:"I don't know yet. If I go, it feels like abandoning the island... The deadline for my answer is Friday, mind you.", gl:"しめ切り (しめきり): a deadline."},
    {t:"narr", text:"In the hall Aoi, as manager, has re-inked every faded label on the mailboxes. Room 205 has a fresh card, still blank. Mrs Satō is at the noticeboard with her pencil."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"fumiko", ja:"あおいさん、205[号室]{ごうしつ}の[方]{かた}がいらっしゃるのは、[明日]{あした}でしたっけ。", en:"Aoi, was it tomorrow that the person for Room 205 is coming?", gl:"～号室 (ごうしつ): room number ～."},
    {t:"line", mood:"think", who:"aoi", ja:"[明日]{あした}のはずですけど…。", en:"It should be tomorrow, but..."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Three knocks: careful ones, from somebody who has checked the address more than once. The cat gets to the door first."},
    {t:"cat", pose:"back", alt:"The cat seen from behind, sitting and facing the front door."},
    {t:"line", mood:"hello", who:"aoi", ja:"はーい、今行きます。", en:"Coming!"},
    {t:"line", mood:"yay", who:"fumiko", ja:"ねこさんの名前が、また一つ[増]{ふ}えそうですね。", en:"It looks as if the cat is about to have one more name.", gl:"増える (ふえる): to increase."},
    {t:"narr", text:"Aoi opens the door. In the kitchen Rodrigo is already getting to his feet. You can only say はじめまして to a person once."},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u12-x1", type:"mcq", q:"In her letter Mrs Satō writes: 私は長い間、あなたが書くのをやめたのだと思っていました。しかし、やめた人はだれもいなかったのです。 What is the point she wants Lorraine to take from it?", options:[
      {t:"Neither of them ever stopped writing", ok:true, why:"Right. The first sentence gives what she used to believe (～と思っていました). しかし turns, and the sentence after the turn carries the point, with ～のです to mark it as the explanation. つまり then sums it up: the fault was the address."},
      {t:"Lorraine stopped writing to her in 1968", why:"That is what she used to think: ～と思っていました puts it in the past. しかし turns away from it."},
      {t:"She herself stopped writing because the family moved", why:"She did move, but she wrote with the new address. やめた人はだれもいなかった: nobody stopped."},
      {t:"She is angry with the people who changed the addresses", why:"She does blame the address, drily, in the next sentence, but there is no anger and nobody is named. The point is that the silence was nobody's choice."}]}},
    {t:"ex", ex:{id:"story-e3u12-x2", type:"mcq", q:"Mariya says 「英語がお[上手]{じょうず}ですね」とおっしゃっています. Whose words are inside the brackets, and how can you tell?", options:[
      {t:"Lorraine's: ～とおっしゃっています reports what someone else is saying, respectfully", ok:true, why:"Right. と marks the quotation and おっしゃる is the respectful *say*, so the speaker is someone Mariya is raising: Lorraine. The compliment is about Mariya, which is why she wanted to skip it."},
      {t:"Mariya's own: she is praising Lorraine's English", why:"Lorraine's English needs no praise from anyone. And Mariya would not use the respectful おっしゃる about her own speech."},
      {t:"Mrs Satō's: Mariya is turning her Japanese into English", why:"In this line the interpreting runs the other way, from Lorraine's English into Japanese. Mrs Satō's messages end ～と[伝]{つた}えてください."},
      {t:"Nobody's: it is a set greeting, like お[久]{ひさ}しぶりです", why:"It is a real remark that Lorraine has just made, quoted with と."}]}},
    {t:"lang", items:["A letter's shape tells you where its point is. Mrs Satō starts from an old belief (～と思っていました), turns with しかし, explains with ～のです, and sums up with つまり. Read the sentence after the turn twice.", "An interpreter's Japanese is full of reporting: 「…」とおっしゃっています, 「…」そうです, 「…」って. Going the other way, Mrs Satō hands each message over with ～と[伝]{つた}えてください.", "Real speech has gaps in it. えーと and あのー buy Mariya time, あ、いえ takes a sentence back, and ～んですけど… and [明日]{あした}のはずですけど… stop early and let the listener finish the thought."]},
    {t:"reflect", q:"For fifty-nine years each of them believed the other had stopped writing, and each thought it was her own fault. Is there someone you lost touch with where the reason may have been as small as an address?"}
  ]}
  ]
};
